WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:14.883
Welcome to the complete walkthrough of your new system. It shows every screen and every button of the office app, then the crew phone app, in twenty-one chapters. You can jump to any chapter from the list under the video.

00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:22.350
Chapter one. A quick tour of the app. The menu, search, Help and where everything lives.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.617
A quick tour of the app.

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:33.950
My day. Every morning starts here: your appointments, follow-ups due, new requests, jobs waiting on a permit and who is on site.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:44.783
Search everything. Type a name, phone, street or an EST-, JOB- or INV- number. ⌘K jumps here from any screen.

00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:51.450
Ask for help any time. Tell it what you want to do and it shows you, step by step, like this.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:59.983
Customers. Every customer and lead. One screen each: phones, addresses, notes, estimates, jobs, invoices.

00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:06.350
Estimates. Every estimate and its follow-ups. Won ones become jobs in one step.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:13.383
Schedule. Crews down the side, days across. Drag work onto a crew; drag it again to move it.

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:18.883
Invoices. Bills, payments, card declines and month-end billing.

00:01:19.383 --> 00:01:24.150
The Guide. Every how-to in one place. Each one has a tour like this.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:34.433
Chapter two. My day. Where every morning starts: today's visits and calls, follow-ups, new requests, permits and who is on site.

00:01:34.633 --> 00:01:36.733
Everything on My day.

00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:49.666
My day: where every morning starts. Today's date, how many appointments you have today, anything overdue and how many crews are on site. Everything on this screen is about you and today.

00:01:50.166 --> 00:02:03.533
Search everything. Type a name, phone, street, or an EST-, JOB- or INV- number and pick the result to open it. ⌘K (Ctrl+K) jumps here from any screen.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:11.200
Help. Ask how to do something in your own words. It finds the tour that fits and shows you on the screen, like this one.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:21.933
Notifications. New assignments, wins and payments for you. The red number counts the unread ones. Click one to open it; Mark all read clears them.

00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:33.433
Crews out today. How many crews are on a job today, out of all your crews. If you see money, this month's wins and the value of estimates out with customers sit beside it.

00:02:33.933 --> 00:02:45.500
New customer. Opens the New customer form right here: name, phones, address, salesperson, and the first appointment if you like. Saving opens the new customer.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:55.766
New appointment. Book a visit, a phone call or a task for anyone. It goes straight onto that person's day. The Appointments tours walk every field.

00:02:56.266 --> 00:03:03.500
Schedule. Opens the Schedule board: crews down the side, days across, and the sold work waiting for a date.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:13.433
Estimates out. Sent estimates still waiting on the customer: the value, or the count if you don't see money. Click the box to open Estimates.

00:03:13.933 --> 00:03:21.833
Won this month. Estimates won since the 1st of the month and how many jobs they made. Click the box to open Jobs.

00:03:22.333 --> 00:03:30.633
To schedule. Pieces of sold work with no crew or start day yet. Click the box to open the Schedule and give them a date.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:42.633
Overdue invoices. What customers owe past the due date, and on how many invoices. Click the box to open Invoices. People who don't see money get Crews out today here.

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:52.166
My day. Your appointments and tasks for today, with anything overdue at the top in red. Add books a new one for you or for someone else.

00:03:52.666 --> 00:04:05.033
Open an appointment. Each line shows the time, what it's for, the customer, place and phone, and the type. A camera means the visit sent notes or photos. Click a line to open it.

00:04:05.533 --> 00:04:17.800
The appointment. When, with whom, the customer (click the name to open them), phone, address and office notes. Below: notes, measurements and photos saved on the visit from the phone.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:31.400
Edit, visit done, mark done. Edit changes it. Visit done · estimate pending keeps an estimate visit open as the reminder to write the quote. Mark done closes it. The tour presses none of them.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:36.300
Close it. The X closes the appointment without changing anything.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:45.000
Edit from the list. The pencil opens the appointment's form straight away, to change the day, time, person or details.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:52.866
Mark it done. The tick marks it done and takes it off your day. Use it once the visit, call or task has happened.

00:04:53.366 --> 00:05:02.500
Next 7 days. Your appointments for the coming week, day by day, so you can plan office time. The lines work the same as in My day.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:15.066
What needs you. Cards here appear only when there is something to do: New from the website, Waiting on a permit (the township hasn't approved yet) and Waiting on a quote (visit done, no estimate).

00:05:15.533 --> 00:05:27.300
New from the website. Website requests waiting for someone. Accept makes the lead (or finds the existing customer) plus a ticket, and opens them. All opens Marketing.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:39.400
Follow-ups. Sent estimates with no answer yet: click one to open it; Sent or Called records the follow-up. When none are due it says the automatic follow-ups are handling them.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:49.866
On site today. Which crew is on which job today, with the customer, place and "day 3 of 5" on longer jobs. Click a line to open the job.

00:05:50.366 --> 00:05:59.766
Automations. Messages the automations sent today, how many are waiting to go and any that failed (red). Click it to open Automations.

00:06:00.266 --> 00:06:08.633
Missed clock-outs. Shows up when someone on a crew forgot to clock out. Fix it on Timesheets before payroll: click it to go there.

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:16.500
Fleet. Truck problems the crews reported from the phone, and trucks overdue for service. Click it to open Fleet.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:24.966
Latest across the business. The eight latest things that happened across all customers. Click a name to open that customer.

00:06:25.517 --> 00:06:35.656
Chapter three. Customers. Every customer and lead, one screen each: booking, calls, notes, estimates, jobs and invoices.

00:06:35.856 --> 00:06:38.189
Everything on Customers.

00:06:38.889 --> 00:06:46.456
Customers. Every customer and lead in one list. The line under the title counts your customers and your leads.

00:06:46.956 --> 00:06:58.023
Export. Saves the list as it is filtered right now as a file for Excel: code, name, phone, email, address, stage, rep and source. Handy for mailings.

00:06:58.489 --> 00:07:05.889
New customer. Opens the New customer form above the list. Let's look at it; the tour doesn't save anything.

00:07:06.389 --> 00:07:14.756
Name. First and last name, or a Company for businesses (leave Company blank for homeowners). Only a name is required.

00:07:15.256 --> 00:07:22.623
Phones and email. Cell phone, another phone and email. Search finds the customer by any of them later.

00:07:23.123 --> 00:07:26.989
Property address. Where the work is: street and number.

00:07:27.489 --> 00:07:34.956
The zip fills the town. Type the 5-digit zip and Town and State fill themselves. You can still change them.

00:07:35.456 --> 00:07:42.923
Billing address. Ticked, invoices go to the property. Untick it to add a different Bill to name and billing address.

00:07:43.423 --> 00:07:54.056
Source, salesperson, CSR. Where the lead came from and who referred them, the Salesperson who owns them and the CSR in the office who looks after them.

00:07:54.556 --> 00:08:07.523
Stage, type, invoicing, terms. Lead, Customer or Inactive; Residential or Commercial; invoiced when work is done or monthly (month-end run); Due on receipt or Net 30.

00:08:08.023 --> 00:08:16.889
Payment and flags. Check or card, the card's last 4 digits only, Do not market (no seasonal emails) and Tax exempt.

00:08:17.389 --> 00:08:23.456
Office notes. Gate codes, dogs, best time to call. They show on the customer's screen.

00:08:23.956 --> 00:08:32.556
Book the first appointment. Tick it to book their first visit in the same step. It goes straight onto that person's day, no second step.

00:08:33.056 --> 00:08:41.156
When and with whom. Date, From and To, and who goes; under it, what it's for and the type. With follows the Salesperson you picked.

00:08:41.656 --> 00:08:49.923
Save customer. Saves the customer (and the appointment) and opens them. Press it yourself when it's real; the tour doesn't save.

00:08:50.423 --> 00:08:55.256
Close the form. The X (or Cancel) closes the form without saving.

00:08:55.756 --> 00:09:06.289
Search customers. Type part of a name, a phone (the last 4 digits work), street, email or C-code. It searches every customer, not only this page.

00:09:06.789 --> 00:09:16.989
Active, leads, customers…. Active is leads and customers together. Leads, Customers, Inactive and All narrow the list; the numbers are the counts.

00:09:17.489 --> 00:09:20.456
Leads only. Let's switch to Leads.

00:09:20.956 --> 00:09:28.623
New lead. On Leads the button says New lead and the form starts as a lead. On Customers it starts as a customer.

00:09:29.123 --> 00:09:33.489
By salesperson. Only the customers of one salesperson.

00:09:33.989 --> 00:09:40.189
By town. Only one town. The number beside each town is how many customers are there.

00:09:40.689 --> 00:09:48.189
Quick filters. Owes money (if you see money), Billed monthly, Open estimates, Do not market, or Demo records.

00:09:48.689 --> 00:10:01.656
The list. Name, address and code, phone, stage, rep, open estimates, balance (money roles: red owed, green credit) and last activity. 50 a page, with Previous / Next below.

00:10:02.156 --> 00:10:12.623
Open a customer. Click anyone to open their screen: details, history, estimates, jobs, invoices and more. "Everything on a customer" shows it all.

00:10:12.972 --> 00:10:15.205
Everything on a customer.

00:10:15.905 --> 00:10:22.539
Open a customer. Click a customer on the list to open their screen. Let's open Bayview Marina.

00:10:23.039 --> 00:10:30.005
Who they are. Code (and Commercial), name and stage, then the property address, phone and email at a glance.

00:10:30.505 --> 00:10:34.072
Back to the list. Goes back to the Customers list.

00:10:34.572 --> 00:10:43.039
Appointment. Books a visit, call or task for them: their name, phone and address come along, and With starts as their salesperson.

00:10:43.539 --> 00:10:51.405
Estimate. Starts a new draft estimate for this customer and opens it. The tour doesn't press it, because it makes the draft.

00:10:51.905 --> 00:10:57.172
Log call. Writes down a phone call, a note or an email on their Timeline.

00:10:57.672 --> 00:11:07.039
Edit. Opens their details in the same form as New customer. The tour "Book, log a call or edit a customer" opens these forms.

00:11:07.539 --> 00:11:19.172
Key facts. Rep, CSR, where they came from, customer since, monthly invoicing and card on file. Do not market and Tax exempt show here in colour when set.

00:11:19.672 --> 00:11:28.139
Timeline. Everything that happened with them, newest first: calls, appointments, estimates, emails, invoices and payments.

00:11:28.639 --> 00:11:35.972
Estimates. Their estimates: number, status, any follow-up due, rep, total and date. Click one to open it.

00:11:36.472 --> 00:11:42.739
Jobs. Their jobs: status, when it runs and the value. Click one to open the job.

00:11:43.239 --> 00:11:50.705
Invoices. Their invoices: date issued, status, total and what's still open. Click one to open it.

00:11:51.205 --> 00:11:57.439
Appointments. Their visits, calls and tasks. The number on the tab counts the open ones.

00:11:57.939 --> 00:12:04.172
New appointment. Books one for this customer, the same as the Appointment button at the top.

00:12:04.672 --> 00:12:13.039
Open one. Click a row to see it: when, who, notes and what came back from the visit (notes, photos), with Edit and Mark done.

00:12:13.539 --> 00:12:19.272
Edit it here. The pencil changes it right here, without going to the Appointments screen.

00:12:19.772 --> 00:12:26.339
Mark done. The tick closes it. A done one shows a Reopen arrow instead, to open it again.

00:12:26.839 --> 00:12:34.539
Photos. Property photos and files kept on the customer, not buried in a job: permits, surveys, drawings.

00:12:35.039 --> 00:12:45.605
Add photos and files. Take photo or Upload file adds one. Each file has Open, and the bin takes it off the customer (the file itself is kept).

00:12:46.105 --> 00:12:56.072
Messages. Every email and text sent to them: follow-ups, reminders, notices, campaigns. Each shows Sent, Queued (with when it goes) or Failed.

00:12:56.572 --> 00:13:06.339
Account balance. What they owe across all open invoices (or their credit), each open invoice (click one to open it) and what they've paid to date.

00:13:06.839 --> 00:13:17.505
Containers. Dumpsters at this customer now: unit, size, address and days out. Drop one books a drop and Pickup books a pickup, both on Deliveries.

00:13:17.972 --> 00:13:29.239
Maintenance plans. Recurring work like lawn care, beds or snow: how often, price and next visit. Add plan (money roles) opens Maintenance for this customer.

00:13:29.739 --> 00:13:41.105
What they get from us. Seasonal marketing emails, payment reminders and text messages. A switch saves the moment you flip it, so change one only when the customer asks.

00:13:41.605 --> 00:13:47.939
Surveys. Their latest survey scores out of 5, with comments. 3 or less shows in red.

00:13:48.439 --> 00:13:52.939
Coming up. Their next open appointments. The tick marks one done.

00:13:53.439 --> 00:14:02.705
Contact. Cell, other phone, email, property, bill-to address and terms. Office notes and other contacts show below when there are any.

00:14:03.056 --> 00:14:06.923
Book a visit, a call back or a task for a customer.

00:14:07.623 --> 00:14:11.723
Find the customer. Search by name, phone or street.

00:14:12.223 --> 00:14:22.856
A new caller?. New customer: name, phones, address (the zip fills the town), CSR and salesperson on one screen, and "Book the first appointment now".

00:14:23.356 --> 00:14:27.123
Open the customer. Click the customer to open them.

00:14:27.623 --> 00:14:32.989
Book it from the customer. Appointment: their name, phone and address come with it.

00:14:33.489 --> 00:14:41.956
Visit, phone call or task. A visit has a time and a place, a phone call shows the number to call, a task is any to-do.

00:14:42.456 --> 00:14:47.023
When. The day, and a time from / to, or leave it at Any time.

00:14:47.523 --> 00:14:53.256
Who goes. Only the people who take appointments are listed (set on Team & crews).

00:14:53.756 --> 00:15:01.289
Save it. Book it puts it on their My day and on their phone. The tour doesn't save anything: press it yourself when it's real.

00:15:01.639 --> 00:15:04.706
Book, log a call or edit a customer.

00:15:05.406 --> 00:15:10.806
Open the customer. It all starts from their screen. Let's open Bayview Marina.

00:15:11.306 --> 00:15:16.372
Book an appointment. Appointment opens the booking form for this customer.

00:15:16.872 --> 00:15:28.572
Visit, phone call or task. Pick what it is first and the fields follow: a call has a call time and who calls, a task can go to anyone. Then What for, Date, time and Notes.

00:15:29.072 --> 00:15:36.772
Who and where come along. Their name, phone and address are filled in already, and With starts as their salesperson.

00:15:37.272 --> 00:15:42.239
Close it. Close it without booking. Book it would put it on that person's day.

00:15:42.739 --> 00:15:47.572
Log a call. Log call writes a conversation down on their Timeline.

00:15:48.072 --> 00:15:53.206
Call, note or email. Phone call, Note or Email: pick what it was.

00:15:53.706 --> 00:15:57.572
What was said. A line or two on what was said or agreed.

00:15:58.072 --> 00:16:03.972
Save it. Save adds it to the Timeline with your name and the time. The tour doesn't press it.

00:16:04.472 --> 00:16:07.639
Close it. The X closes it without saving.

00:16:08.139 --> 00:16:12.972
Edit their details. Edit opens everything about them in one form.

00:16:13.472 --> 00:16:25.639
Change stage and billing. The same fields as New customer. Move a lead to Customer or Inactive here, switch to monthly invoicing, change terms, salesperson or CSR.

00:16:26.106 --> 00:16:31.339
Save changes. Saves and updates their screen. The tour doesn't save.

00:16:31.839 --> 00:16:35.339
Close it. Closes the form; nothing changed.

00:16:35.839 --> 00:16:43.472
Start an estimate. Estimate makes a new draft estimate for them and opens it to write. Press it when you're ready to quote.

00:16:44.022 --> 00:16:52.838
Chapter four. Appointments. Visits, phone calls and tasks: booking them, the lists, and sending one to someone.

00:16:53.038 --> 00:16:55.305
Everything on Appointments.

00:16:56.005 --> 00:17:05.671
Appointments. Sales visits, call-backs, collections and tasks for everyone. Each one sits on someone's day, so nothing is left without a date.

00:17:06.138 --> 00:17:10.271
New appointment. Opens the booking form. Let's have a look.

00:17:10.771 --> 00:17:21.438
Visit, phone call or task. Pick what it is, then the customer, what for, date, time and who. The tour "Book a visit, a phone call or a task" walks every field.

00:17:21.905 --> 00:17:24.605
Close it. Close it without booking.

00:17:25.105 --> 00:17:30.771
Mine. Your own open appointments and tasks. The numbers on the tabs are counts.

00:17:31.271 --> 00:17:35.171
Search. Find one by subject, customer or place.

00:17:35.671 --> 00:17:41.338
By type. Estimate visit, Site visit, Call back, Collection, Service or Other.

00:17:41.838 --> 00:17:48.871
Grouped by day. Overdue first in red, then Today, Tomorrow and the days after, with how many on each.

00:17:49.371 --> 00:17:59.471
One appointment. The time (or Any time), what it's for, the customer, place and phone, a camera if the visit sent notes or photos, the type and who has it.

00:17:59.971 --> 00:18:02.971
Open it. Click the line to open it.

00:18:03.471 --> 00:18:10.938
The details. When, with whom, the customer (click the name to open them), phone, address and the office notes.

00:18:11.438 --> 00:18:20.605
From the visit. Notes, measurements and photos the salesperson saved on the visit from the phone. Until then it says nothing came back yet.

00:18:21.105 --> 00:18:32.905
Edit, visit done, mark done. Edit changes it. Visit done · estimate pending puts an estimate visit on Waiting on a quote. Mark done closes it. The tour presses none of them.

00:18:33.405 --> 00:18:35.938
Close it. The X closes it.

00:18:36.438 --> 00:18:42.338
Edit. The pencil opens the form to change the day, time, person or details.

00:18:42.838 --> 00:18:47.605
Mark done. The tick marks it done. It moves to Done · 30 days.

00:18:48.105 --> 00:18:51.605
Everyone. Every open appointment, whoever has it.

00:18:52.105 --> 00:18:58.338
By person. Pick one person to see only theirs. It isn't on Mine, which is always yours.

00:18:58.838 --> 00:19:09.071
Waiting on a quote. Estimate visits marked Visit done · estimate pending: the quote is still to write. Mark the visit done once the estimate has gone out.

00:19:09.571 --> 00:19:17.171
Overdue. Everything past its date and still open, for everyone. Call, move it with the pencil, or mark it done.

00:19:17.671 --> 00:19:25.038
Done · 30 days. What was finished in the last 30 days, newest first. The arrow on a line reopens it.

00:19:25.388 --> 00:19:28.455
Book a visit, a phone call or a task.

00:19:29.155 --> 00:19:38.621
New appointment. Opens the booking form. Visits, phone calls and tasks all start here (or from a customer, with their details filled in).

00:19:39.121 --> 00:19:45.788
What is it?. Start with what it is: a Visit, a Phone call or a Task. The form changes to fit.

00:19:46.288 --> 00:19:52.555
Visit. A visit has a place and a time: estimate visits, site visits and service calls.

00:19:53.055 --> 00:20:00.355
The customer. Type a name, phone or street and pick them. Leave it empty for an internal task or meeting.

00:20:00.855 --> 00:20:07.621
What for. A short line everyone understands, like "Estimate visit · back patio". It's required.

00:20:08.121 --> 00:20:16.188
Type. Estimate visit, Site visit or Service. After an estimate visit it can be marked Visit done · estimate pending.

00:20:16.655 --> 00:20:23.255
Priority. Low, Normal, High or Urgent. High and Urgent show a red tag on the lists.

00:20:23.755 --> 00:20:29.588
Date. The day it happens. It's also the due date, so it's on that person's day straight away.

00:20:30.088 --> 00:20:35.855
From and To. Pick a start and the end follows an hour later, or leave it at Any time.

00:20:36.355 --> 00:20:42.455
With. Who goes. Only people who take appointments are listed (set on Team & crews).

00:20:42.955 --> 00:20:48.421
Notes. Anything the person should know: a gate code, what the customer asked for.

00:20:48.921 --> 00:20:51.988
Phone call. Now let's make it a phone call.

00:20:52.488 --> 00:21:03.455
Call at and who calls. A call has one time (15 minutes) and Who calls. Its type is Call back or Collection, and the call's subject goes in What the call is about.

00:21:03.955 --> 00:21:08.988
Task. And a task: any to-do, an internal meeting, an order to place.

00:21:09.488 --> 00:21:18.355
Anyone, crews included. A task can go to anyone in the company. It shows on their My day and their phone until they mark it done.

00:21:18.855 --> 00:21:25.821
Book it. Book it saves it onto that person's day; Cancel throws it away. The tour doesn't save anything.

00:21:26.321 --> 00:21:29.855
Close it. The X closes the form without booking.

00:21:30.205 --> 00:21:33.505
Give someone a task (to-do, internal meeting).

00:21:34.205 --> 00:21:39.872
New appointment. Tasks, visits and calls all start here (or from a customer).

00:21:40.372 --> 00:21:46.438
Choose Task. A task is any to-do: an internal meeting, an order to place, a follow-up.

00:21:46.938 --> 00:21:55.405
Anyone, crews included. Give it to anyone in the company. It shows on their phone under My appointments until they mark it done.

00:21:55.905 --> 00:22:00.072
Save it. Book it when it's real. The tour doesn't save anything.

00:22:00.422 --> 00:22:03.089
Email an appointment to someone.

00:22:03.789 --> 00:22:07.055
Open an appointment. Click any appointment.

00:22:07.555 --> 00:22:23.855
Email it. Sends the details to anyone: when, the customer, their phone and address, and the notes. Click it and a small form opens: the address to send it to, a note from you if you like (Can you cover this one?), and Send. It is logged on the appointment.

00:22:24.405 --> 00:22:36.613
Chapter five. Estimates. From the first visit to the won job: sections, measuring, terms, selections, sending, follow-ups, won or lost, the customer copy.

00:22:36.813 --> 00:22:39.080
Everything on Estimates.

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:48.846
Estimates. Every estimate in one list, from the first visit to the won job: drafts, ones out with customers, follow-ups, won and lost.

00:22:49.313 --> 00:22:55.780
Start a new estimate. New estimate first asks who it is for. The tour opens it to show you.

00:22:56.280 --> 00:23:04.746
Find the customer. Type a name, phone or street and click the customer: a new draft estimate opens for them straight away.

00:23:05.246 --> 00:23:14.680
Not a customer yet?. Add a new customer opens the customer form right here. Saving it adds the customer and opens their new estimate.

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:21.946
Name. First and last name, or a company name for commercial work. Only a name is required.

00:23:22.446 --> 00:23:30.013
Phones and email. Cell phone, other phone and email. The email is where the estimate and its follow-ups go.

00:23:30.513 --> 00:23:39.680
Property address. Where the work is. Type the zip and the town fills itself in. Untick "Bill to the property address" if the bill goes somewhere else.

00:23:40.180 --> 00:23:52.046
Source, salesperson and CSR. How they found you, who referred them, their salesperson and the office CSR. Stage, type, invoicing and payment terms sit just below.

00:23:52.546 --> 00:24:02.213
Book the visit in the same go. Tick it to put the estimate visit on the salesperson's day with the same save: date, time, who goes and what for.

00:24:02.680 --> 00:24:09.413
Save customer. Saves the customer and opens their new estimate. The tour doesn't save anything.

00:24:09.913 --> 00:24:13.913
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving.

00:24:14.413 --> 00:24:21.480
Drafts. Estimates written but not sent yet, and what they are worth. Click it to see them on the Open tab.

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:27.646
Out with customers. Sent and waiting on a yes or no, with their total value.

00:24:28.146 --> 00:24:37.380
In follow-up. Sent estimates with a follow-up due or planned. With automatic follow-ups on, the reminder emails go by themselves.

00:24:37.880 --> 00:24:44.980
Won this year. What you won this year, how many jobs that is, and your close rate (won out of won plus lost).

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:53.046
Open. The list starts on Open: drafts, and sent estimates still waiting on an answer. The number is how many.

00:24:53.513 --> 00:24:59.580
Follow-ups. Sent estimates with a follow-up due, or the next automatic email planned.

00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:08.546
Who to chase. The Status column says Follow up, 2nd follow-up or Call them, and shows the next automatic step with its date.

00:25:09.046 --> 00:25:12.613
Won. Every estimate the customer said yes to.

00:25:13.113 --> 00:25:18.346
Straight to the job. Job opens the job that was made from that estimate.

00:25:18.846 --> 00:25:24.646
Lost. Lost and expired estimates, with the reason given when they were marked lost.

00:25:25.146 --> 00:25:28.346
All. Every estimate, whatever its status.

00:25:28.846 --> 00:25:35.713
Search. Type an estimate number, a title, the customer or the town: the list narrows as you type.

00:25:36.213 --> 00:25:42.280
Filter by rep. Show one salesperson's estimates only. Any rep shows everyone's.

00:25:42.780 --> 00:25:53.646
The columns. Estimate number, title and customer; status; rep; total; and when it was sent. A long list shows 50 at a time with Previous and Next.

00:25:54.146 --> 00:26:00.646
Open one. Click any row to open the estimate. The tour "Everything on an estimate" walks through it.

00:26:00.996 --> 00:26:03.296
Everything on an estimate.

00:26:03.996 --> 00:26:09.563
Open an estimate. Click a row to open the estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:26:10.063 --> 00:26:19.396
Back to the customer. The customer's name above the title opens their page: phones, notes, and all their estimates, jobs and invoices.

00:26:19.896 --> 00:26:30.629
Where it stands. The number and status sit above the title. Here: the status (Draft, Sent, Won, Lost), any follow-up due, the address, phone and when it was sent.

00:26:31.129 --> 00:26:36.296
Customer view. Switch to see the estimate exactly as the customer gets it.

00:26:36.796 --> 00:26:49.496
The real document. The saved copy the customer receives by email, as a PDF or on paper: sections, totals, add-ons and terms. Print / PDF is just above it.

00:26:49.996 --> 00:26:53.529
Back to Build. Build is where you write the estimate.

00:26:54.029 --> 00:27:03.596
Save. Saves sections, prices and details. "Unsaved changes" shows beside it until you do. ⌘S or Ctrl+S saves too.

00:27:04.063 --> 00:27:16.496
Send. Opens the send choices: email the online link (best), email it, print or save as PDF, or "I sent it another way". Each marks it Sent and starts the follow-ups.

00:27:16.996 --> 00:27:27.063
Won. When the customer says yes. One step makes the contract, the payment schedule and the job. The tour "Mark an estimate won or lost" shows it.

00:27:27.529 --> 00:27:36.596
Lost. When they say no: pick why (price, someone else, timing…). It stays for the close-rate report, and Reopen brings it back as a draft.

00:27:37.063 --> 00:27:47.996
Measure. Opens a satellite photo of the property. Trace the patio, driveway, beds or wall line; back here a Measured card turns each area into a section.

00:27:48.496 --> 00:27:57.096
Duplicate. Copies this estimate as a new draft for the same customer, e.g. a second option, and opens the copy.

00:27:57.596 --> 00:28:08.063
Sections. Each section is one line the customer sees (Patio, Walls, Lighting…) with its own total. The labor price and the materials go inside it.

00:28:08.563 --> 00:28:17.363
Taxable or Tax exempt. One click switches the section between Taxable and Tax exempt; the sales tax in Totals follows.

00:28:17.863 --> 00:28:29.229
Materials, hidden or shown. The materials in a section. Unticked lines are hidden: the customer sees only the section total. Cost and price give you the margin.

00:28:29.729 --> 00:28:38.663
Optional add-ons. A dashed section is an optional add-on: priced on its own and left out of the total until the customer takes it.

00:28:39.163 --> 00:28:49.929
Add a section. Search the catalogue: a service brings its price, unit, crew-hours, tax setting and its kit of materials. Blank section starts an empty one.

00:28:50.429 --> 00:28:58.963
Totals. Subtotal, sales tax at this estimate's rate and the total. Optional add-ons are shown apart, not in the total.

00:28:59.463 --> 00:29:10.029
Customer copy. Open the customer copy shows the document full width; Print / PDF prints it or saves a PDF you can attach to your own email.

00:29:10.529 --> 00:29:20.996
Contract terms. The payment schedule the contract gets, what each payment comes to, and the NJ ST-8 capital improvement switch (no sales tax).

00:29:21.496 --> 00:29:33.296
Online estimate. The customer's link: Sent, Opened, Signed. They tick add-ons, initial the terms and sign; signing makes the job, contract and deposit invoice.

00:29:33.796 --> 00:29:43.496
Follow-ups. What the automatic follow-up does next and when, with an on / off switch for this estimate. Emails and texts about it are listed here.

00:29:43.996 --> 00:29:54.163
Margin. Materials at cost plus crew-hours at your labor cost: cost, gross profit, margin % and crew-hours. Never shown to the customer.

00:29:54.629 --> 00:30:05.463
Material selections. What the customer picked at the supplier: pavers, wall block, caps, steps… It goes on the selection sheet, the proposal and the work order.

00:30:05.963 --> 00:30:16.929
Details. Title, salesperson, valid until, tax %, a message to the customer, an office note they never see, and terms. Save keeps your changes.

00:30:17.280 --> 00:30:19.647
Write and send an estimate.

00:30:20.347 --> 00:30:24.980
A new estimate. Start here, or from the customer with New estimate.

00:30:25.480 --> 00:30:28.913
Open one. Let's look inside an estimate.

00:30:29.413 --> 00:30:40.180
One section per scope. Paver patio, Lighting, Walls … The customer sees each section with its total; materials inside stay hidden unless you tick them.

00:30:40.680 --> 00:30:48.247
Taxable or tax exempt. One click switches the section between Taxable and Tax exempt; the tax follows.

00:30:48.713 --> 00:30:57.280
Measure on the aerial photo. Trace the patio, driveway, beds or wall line; the areas go onto the estimate in one click.

00:30:57.780 --> 00:31:03.413
Pavers and colours. The customer's picks, and the Selection sheet for them to sign.

00:31:03.913 --> 00:31:09.447
What the customer gets. Open or print exactly what the customer receives.

00:31:09.947 --> 00:31:20.613
Send it. Top right: Email it (or Email the link again / Send the update once it has gone out) and Print / PDF. Follow-ups due then show on My day.

00:31:20.963 --> 00:31:24.896
Build an estimate: sections, materials, add-ons.

00:31:25.596 --> 00:31:31.263
Open an estimate. Sections are built on the estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:31:31.763 --> 00:31:43.030
The section bar. Each section is one line on the estimate. Its bar holds the name, the tax switch, the section total and the tools to fold, move or remove it.

00:31:43.530 --> 00:31:52.830
Fold it away. The arrow folds a section to one line so a long estimate is easy to read. The tax switch and the total stay visible.

00:31:53.330 --> 00:32:02.396
Section name. What the customer reads as the line title, e.g. Paver patio. Every section needs a name before you can save.

00:32:02.896 --> 00:32:14.530
Taxable or Tax exempt. One click switches it; the sales tax follows. The Taxable tick inside the section does the same. Catalogue services bring their own setting.

00:32:15.030 --> 00:32:22.663
Section total. Quantity × labor price, plus every material line at its price. It updates as you type.

00:32:23.163 --> 00:32:30.263
Move up or down. The arrows change the order the customer reads the sections in. Nothing is deleted.

00:32:30.763 --> 00:32:38.363
Remove a section. Takes the section and its materials off (it asks first). Nothing is final until you press Save.

00:32:38.863 --> 00:32:46.496
What the customer reads. Describe the work in plain words. This text is printed under the section name on the estimate.

00:32:46.996 --> 00:32:57.363
Quantity and unit. How many, and of what (sq ft, job, ea, ft). After you measure, "Use a measurement" buttons appear here and fill both in one click.

00:32:57.863 --> 00:33:04.396
Labor price per unit. Your price for the work, per unit. The materials below are added on top.

00:33:04.896 --> 00:33:12.363
Crew-hours (budget). How long the crew needs. It sizes the job on the Schedule and feeds the Margin card.

00:33:12.863 --> 00:33:21.963
Optional add-on. Tick it for an extra the customer can choose, like lighting. It's priced apart and kept out of the total until they take it.

00:33:22.463 --> 00:33:31.296
Note for the crew. Gas line, access, where to dump spoils… It goes on the job and the work order, never on the customer's copy.

00:33:31.796 --> 00:33:41.963
Materials. Material, quantity, unit, your cost, the customer's price and the line amount. Cost stays inside the office; it drives the margin.

00:33:42.430 --> 00:33:53.563
Hidden or shown lines. Unticked (the default), a line is hidden: the customer sees only the section total. Tick Show to list it on their copy, without its price.

00:33:54.063 --> 00:34:00.230
Reorder or remove lines. The arrows move a line up or down; the x removes it.

00:34:00.730 --> 00:34:08.896
Add a material. Search the catalogue by name or category and pick one: it comes in with its unit, cost and price.

00:34:09.396 --> 00:34:16.430
Blank line. For a material that isn't in the catalogue: type the name, quantity, cost and price yourself.

00:34:16.930 --> 00:34:24.930
An optional add-on. Dashed and marked Optional. The customer ticks it on the online link, or you tick it when you press Won.

00:34:25.430 --> 00:34:36.196
Add a section from the catalogue. Pick a service: it brings its price, unit, crew-hours and tax setting, plus its kit of materials (hidden unless the kit says show).

00:34:36.696 --> 00:34:40.563
Blank section. An empty section to fill in yourself.

00:34:41.063 --> 00:34:48.763
Totals. Subtotal, sales tax on the taxable sections and the total, plus "Optional add-ons (not in total)".

00:34:49.263 --> 00:34:56.696
Margin. Cost, gross profit, margin % and crew-hours, as you build. Never shown to the customer.

00:34:57.196 --> 00:35:06.130
Save it. Nothing is kept until you press Save (or ⌘S / Ctrl+S); "Unsaved changes" reminds you. The tour doesn't save.

00:35:06.480 --> 00:35:08.547
Everything on Measure.

00:35:09.247 --> 00:35:14.780
Open the estimate. Measuring starts from an estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:35:15.280 --> 00:35:22.147
Measure. Opens the Measure screen for this estimate (it saves your changes first). The tour opens it.

00:35:22.647 --> 00:35:27.747
Which estimate. The estimate number and the customer you are measuring for.

00:35:28.247 --> 00:35:37.313
The property address. The satellite photo opens on this address. With no address on the customer, search for the house on the map instead.

00:35:37.780 --> 00:35:46.947
Back to the estimate. Goes back to the estimate. What you drew is kept only if you save it first with Save and go to the estimate, under the map.

00:35:47.447 --> 00:35:52.013
Customer. Opens the customer: phones, notes, gate codes.

00:35:52.513 --> 00:36:02.213
How to draw. Under this note is the satellite photo. Pick what you are measuring, then tap the corners. Tap the first corner again to close the shape.

00:36:02.713 --> 00:36:14.113
What you can measure. Patio / pavers, Driveway, Walkway, Lawn and Beds / mulch as areas in square feet; Wall / edging as a line in feet. Search moves the map.

00:36:14.613 --> 00:36:22.547
Fix and cut out. Drag a corner to adjust a shape. Use Cut-out to take a pool, the house or a bed out of an area.

00:36:23.047 --> 00:36:32.713
Save it onto the estimate. Under the map, What you measured adds it up by kind as you draw. Save and go to the estimate keeps it and takes you back.

00:36:33.213 --> 00:36:43.547
Then, on the estimate. A Measured card lists each area: Add makes it a section, or "Use a measurement" in a section fills its quantity. Open comes back here.

00:36:43.896 --> 00:36:47.963
Payment schedule, tax and ST-8 on an estimate.

00:36:48.663 --> 00:36:54.229
Open the estimate. Terms are set on each estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:36:54.729 --> 00:37:02.329
Contract terms. What the customer signs up to if they accept: the payment schedule and whether sales tax applies.

00:37:02.829 --> 00:37:11.996
Pick the payment schedule. The schedules from Settings; the default for this kind of work is already picked. Choosing one saves it on the estimate.

00:37:12.463 --> 00:37:21.696
Each payment, worked out. Deposit, start of work, completion… with what each comes to and when it's due. They follow the total as you edit.

00:37:22.196 --> 00:37:36.163
A custom split. "Custom for this estimate…" opens an editor: start from 30/60/10, 50/50 or deposit + final; set %, fixed $ or the balance, and when each is due.

00:37:36.663 --> 00:37:50.263
NJ ST-8: no sales tax. Switch on for new construction (patio, wall, driveway): no sales tax, and the customer signs an ST-8 to keep on the job. It takes effect at once.

00:37:50.763 --> 00:37:58.329
Terms added from Settings. The standard terms from Settings that print on this estimate. Click the line to read them.

00:37:58.796 --> 00:38:09.596
Tax in the totals. Sales tax is the estimate's Tax % on the taxable sections only. Tax exempt sections, and ST-8 jobs, pay none.

00:38:10.096 --> 00:38:16.263
Tax %. The sales tax rate for this estimate. Change it only for a special case.

00:38:16.763 --> 00:38:21.629
Valid until. How long the price holds. It prints on the estimate.

00:38:22.129 --> 00:38:29.196
Terms for this estimate. Extra terms for this estimate only, printed with it. Press Save to keep them.

00:38:29.546 --> 00:38:32.413
Material selections and approval.

00:38:33.113 --> 00:38:39.379
Open the estimate. Selections are kept on the estimate. The tour opens one that has some.

00:38:39.879 --> 00:38:48.313
Material selections. The customer's picks at the supplier (the Cedar Bridge form). Anyone working on the estimate can fill them in.

00:38:48.813 --> 00:38:57.246
The picks, group by group. Pavers, Walls & steps, Stone, edging & extras, and Upgrades. Empty groups are left out.

00:38:57.746 --> 00:39:06.313
The customer's approval. Waiting on the customer until they approve. If the picks change after that, they go back for a new approval.

00:39:06.813 --> 00:39:13.379
Record their approval. Opens a short form for when they approve. The tour opens it to show you.

00:39:13.879 --> 00:39:17.746
Who approved. Their name, filled in with the customer's.

00:39:18.246 --> 00:39:24.746
When and how. The date, and how: signed form, email, in person, by phone or online.

00:39:25.246 --> 00:39:32.646
Save approval. Keeps it; the card then shows Approved, by whom and how, with Undo. The tour doesn't save.

00:39:33.146 --> 00:39:36.213
Cancel. Closes the form without saving.

00:39:36.713 --> 00:39:44.046
The selection sheet. The selection form in your letterhead, for the customer to check and sign. The tour opens it.

00:39:44.546 --> 00:39:52.546
Check it. Every pick, laid out like the supplier's form. Print / PDF prints it or saves a PDF to email.

00:39:53.046 --> 00:39:55.913
Close it. The x closes the sheet.

00:39:56.379 --> 00:40:02.846
Edit the picks. Edit (Add selections when there are none) opens the whole form above the estimate.

00:40:03.346 --> 00:40:08.846
Pavers. Manufacturer, style, colour, the field paver and the border paver.

00:40:09.346 --> 00:40:14.713
Walls and steps. Wall block, wall caps, step treads and pool coping.

00:40:15.213 --> 00:40:23.379
Stone, edging and extras. Stepping stones, stone veneer, edge / curbstone, property stone and any extras.

00:40:23.879 --> 00:40:31.946
Upgrades. Paver or wall block upgrades, the upgrade colour (Standard, Plus, Premier) and size, or any other upgrade.

00:40:32.446 --> 00:40:39.179
Attach the signed form. Upload the customer's signed sheet; it's kept with the selections when you save.

00:40:39.679 --> 00:40:46.746
Save selections. Keeps the picks on the estimate, the proposal and the work order. The tour doesn't save.

00:40:47.246 --> 00:40:51.713
Close the form. The x (or Cancel) closes it without saving.

00:40:52.063 --> 00:40:55.496
Material selections and the selection sheet.

00:40:56.196 --> 00:41:00.263
Open the estimate. Selections live on the estimate.

00:41:00.763 --> 00:41:10.463
The customer's picks. Add selections: field and border paver, wall block, caps, steps, coping, upgrades. Record approval when they sign.

00:41:10.813 --> 00:41:13.546
Send an estimate and follow it up.

00:41:14.246 --> 00:41:19.746
Open the estimate. Sending starts on the estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:41:20.246 --> 00:41:32.580
Send (or Send again). Opens: Email the online link (best: they sign on their phone), Email it, Print / save as PDF, or I sent it another way. Each marks it Sent.

00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:38.146
Check it first. The Customer copy card shows exactly what they will get.

00:41:38.646 --> 00:41:42.780
Open the customer copy. The tour opens it to show you.

00:41:43.280 --> 00:41:52.913
The customer's copy. Your letterhead, each section with its total, shown materials, optional add-ons and the terms: exactly what they receive.

00:41:53.413 --> 00:42:00.613
Print / PDF. Opens the print window. Choose Save as PDF to attach it to your own email.

00:42:01.113 --> 00:42:04.080
Close it. The x closes the copy.

00:42:04.580 --> 00:42:13.413
The online estimate. The best way to send: the customer opens a link, ticks the add-ons they want, initials the terms and signs.

00:42:13.913 --> 00:42:22.280
Sent, Opened, Signed. Where the customer is. Signing makes the job, the contract and the deposit invoice by itself.

00:42:22.780 --> 00:42:26.746
The link. How many add-ons it offers, and the link itself.

00:42:27.246 --> 00:42:32.713
Copy the link. Copies it, to paste into a text message or your own email.

00:42:33.213 --> 00:42:37.713
See it as they do. Opens the link as the customer sees it.

00:42:38.213 --> 00:42:48.480
Email the link again. Re-sends the same link. If you change the estimate after it went out, a yellow note offers Send the update, which replaces their link.

00:42:48.980 --> 00:42:59.746
Follow-ups. After sending, reminders go by themselves: email 1, email 2, then a call ticket for the office. Days are set in Automations.

00:43:00.246 --> 00:43:10.580
Automatic on or off. Switch automatic follow-ups off for this estimate only; it takes effect at once. The company-wide switch is on Automations.

00:43:11.080 --> 00:43:20.713
What happens next. The next automatic step and when it goes. Messages already sent are listed under it. Follow-ups due also show on My day.

00:43:21.063 --> 00:43:23.730
Mark an estimate won or lost.

00:43:24.430 --> 00:43:29.763
Open the estimate. The one the customer answered. The tour opens this one.

00:43:30.263 --> 00:43:40.030
They said yes. Press Won when they accept on the phone, by email or in person. It saves your changes first. The tour opens it to show you.

00:43:40.530 --> 00:43:48.596
Which add-ons they took. Tick each optional add-on they want. The contract total and the payments below change as you tick.

00:43:49.096 --> 00:44:00.230
What one step creates. The contract (signature required over the amount set in Settings), the payment schedule with each amount, and a job with one work item per section.

00:44:00.730 --> 00:44:08.230
Create the job. Press it when it's real: the job opens next and waits on the Schedule. The tour doesn't press it.

00:44:08.730 --> 00:44:13.096
Close. Cancel or the x closes it; nothing changes.

00:44:13.596 --> 00:44:24.563
They said no. Lost asks why (price, went with someone else, timing / next year, no response, changed plans, other) plus details. It counts in the close rate.

00:44:25.063 --> 00:44:28.163
Won estimates. Now one that was won.

00:44:28.663 --> 00:44:32.330
Open a won estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:44:32.830 --> 00:44:40.830
The won banner. When it was won and the job number. The job, the contract and the payment schedule were all made from it.

00:44:41.330 --> 00:44:47.296
Open the job. Goes to the job: schedule it, order materials, follow the payments.

00:44:47.796 --> 00:44:58.230
A record now. A won estimate is locked: sections read as a record and each add-on says taken or not taken. Duplicate it if more work comes up.

00:44:58.730 --> 00:45:02.030
Lost estimates. And one that was lost.

00:45:02.530 --> 00:45:06.330
Open a lost estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:45:06.830 --> 00:45:11.530
Why it was lost. The day it was marked lost and the reason given.

00:45:12.030 --> 00:45:20.630
Reopen. If they come back (or it expired), Reopen makes it a draft again so you can update it and send it. The tour doesn't press it.

00:45:20.980 --> 00:45:25.513
The customer said yes: contract, payment schedule and job.

00:45:26.213 --> 00:45:29.980
Open the estimate. The one the customer accepted.

00:45:30.480 --> 00:45:35.647
Won. Press Won when they accept: on the phone, by email or in person.

00:45:36.147 --> 00:45:44.713
One step makes it all. The contract, the payment schedule and the job, with a work item per section. Tick the add-ons they took.

00:45:45.180 --> 00:45:51.847
Create the job. Press it when it's real: the job then waits on the Schedule. The tour doesn't press it.

00:45:52.196 --> 00:45:56.396
Invoice an estimate in one click (small jobs, cleanups).

00:45:57.096 --> 00:46:02.596
Open the estimate. A small job or a cleanup that's done? Open its estimate.

00:46:03.096 --> 00:46:21.596
Invoice it. Marks the estimate won, so the job is made and commission and job costing follow it, then makes a draft invoice for the whole amount, line by line as the customer saw it. You check the draft, then email or print it. On a won estimate the green banner has Invoice the job.

00:46:22.096 --> 00:46:30.963
Design pictures. Drawings or photos of the design. Add puts them in the proposal under Your design, with a caption if you like.

00:46:31.463 --> 00:46:43.429
The customer copy. Open the customer copy shows the A4 pages exactly as the customer gets them. Print or PDF prints them, or saves a PDF to attach.

00:46:43.780 --> 00:46:47.847
The customer copy: A4 invoices and proposals.

00:46:48.547 --> 00:46:51.647
Open an invoice. Click any invoice.

00:46:52.147 --> 00:47:07.180
What the customer gets. The invoice exactly as it's printed and emailed: A4 pages, with the invoice total, what's paid, what's due and when it was issued across the top. The account balance stays in its own box at the bottom.

00:47:07.680 --> 00:47:11.480
Open full size. The pages at real size.

00:47:11.980 --> 00:47:23.747
Print or PDF. Print it, or choose Save as PDF in the print window to attach it to an email. Proposals work the same way, from the estimate's Customer copy card.

00:47:24.296 --> 00:47:33.944
Chapter six. Marketing. Email campaigns, templates designed with AI or a ready layout, and the cleanup sign-ups.

00:47:34.144 --> 00:47:36.377
Everything on Marketing.

00:47:37.077 --> 00:47:45.877
Marketing. Seasonal emails to the right customers, your Spring and Fall cleanup sign-ups, and requests from your website, on one screen.

00:47:46.377 --> 00:47:55.544
The numbers. Customers you can reach by email, how many opted out, campaigns sent, cleanup sign-ups waiting and new website requests.

00:47:56.044 --> 00:48:06.044
New campaign. Owner and office: starts a blank campaign. Most start from a season card instead. "Write and send an email campaign" walks through it.

00:48:06.544 --> 00:48:17.977
Live email is off. While this shows, you can write and test campaigns but nothing goes to customers. Live email is switched on in Automations → Sending setup.

00:48:18.477 --> 00:48:22.877
Campaigns. Every campaign you've written, and the season starters.

00:48:23.377 --> 00:48:34.411
A campaign. Name, status (Draft, Scheduled, Sending, Sent, Stopped), subject, who made it and when. While sending, a bar shows how many went, wait or failed.

00:48:34.911 --> 00:48:44.677
Open a draft. Opens a draft to finish it. While one is going out, Stop is here instead: emails already sent stay sent, the rest are cancelled.

00:48:45.177 --> 00:48:51.411
Duplicate. Copies a campaign as a new draft: last fall's email, ready for this fall.

00:48:51.911 --> 00:48:57.911
Delete a draft. Deletes a draft you don't need (it asks first). Only drafts can be deleted.

00:48:58.411 --> 00:49:09.477
Start from a season. Spring or fall cleanup, paver sealing, next year's project, "still thinking it over?" and maintenance plans: each brings its wording and who should get it.

00:49:09.944 --> 00:49:17.344
Cleanup sign-ups. Your Spring and Fall Service Request Forms and everyone who signed up, in the order received.

00:49:17.844 --> 00:49:28.411
Your forms. One card per season with the sign-ups waiting. The link for your website and emails, with Copy link, appears here once the online forms are on.

00:49:28.911 --> 00:49:35.477
See the form. Shows the form question for question, as customers see it. The tour opens it.

00:49:35.977 --> 00:49:47.044
What customers fill in. Name, phone, address, the services they want, meet a manager or just a quote, the date they'd like, and any billing or contact changes.

00:49:47.511 --> 00:49:50.477
Close it. The x closes the preview.

00:49:50.977 --> 00:50:00.544
Someone calls instead. Take a phone sign-up asks the same questions and puts them in line. "Take a cleanup sign-up on the phone" shows the form.

00:50:01.011 --> 00:50:06.511
Spring or Fall. Switches the list below between the Spring and the Fall sign-ups.

00:50:07.011 --> 00:50:18.311
In the order received. Number in line, when and how it came in, the customer, what they want, estimate style, preferred date, and flags: auto-pay call, billing change, note.

00:50:18.811 --> 00:50:28.177
Accept. Makes the visit: "meet a manager" becomes an estimate visit to book, "just send a quote" a stop-by. New people are added as leads.

00:50:28.677 --> 00:50:33.544
Dismiss. The x takes a sign-up off the list (a duplicate, a test).

00:50:34.044 --> 00:50:39.711
Website requests. Requests from the form on your website and from campaign buttons.

00:50:40.211 --> 00:50:48.611
The request form. Its link, for your website and campaign buttons, with Copy link. It shows once the public form is switched on.

00:50:49.111 --> 00:50:58.877
A new request. Name, town, phone, email, the services they want, their message and the best time. Ones that look like spam are flagged.

00:50:59.377 --> 00:51:07.144
Accept. Matches an existing customer or adds a new lead, makes a ticket for the visit, and opens the customer.

00:51:07.644 --> 00:51:15.744
Dismiss. Spam or not for you. Accepted and dismissed requests move to a Handled list below, with who handled them.

00:51:16.094 --> 00:51:18.861
Write and send an email campaign.

00:51:19.527 --> 00:51:22.527
Campaigns. Campaigns are written here.

00:51:23.027 --> 00:51:33.761
Start from a season. Each card brings the wording, a button and who should get it. New campaign starts blank; Open finishes a draft. The tour opens this one.

00:51:34.261 --> 00:51:39.894
The email. What the customer reads. The preview on the right changes as you type.

00:51:40.394 --> 00:51:46.561
Campaign name. Only the office sees it, e.g. Spring cleanup 2027.

00:51:47.061 --> 00:51:53.361
Subject line. What they see in their inbox. {first_name} becomes each customer's first name.

00:51:53.861 --> 00:52:03.061
The message. Your own wording. A blank line starts a new paragraph; {first_name}, {company} and {company_phone} are filled in for each customer.

00:52:03.561 --> 00:52:11.727
The button. The big button in the email, e.g. Book a spring cleanup, and its link: your request form once it is set up.

00:52:12.227 --> 00:52:17.661
Design. How it looks in the inbox: layout, colour, pictures and headline.

00:52:18.161 --> 00:52:27.394
Layout. Photo header puts a wide photo of your work on top; Colour banner a coloured band with the headline; Plain is a simple letter.

00:52:27.894 --> 00:52:36.561
Header picture. Paste a picture link or press Upload. A wide landscape photo, at least 1200 px across, looks best.

00:52:37.061 --> 00:52:41.127
Colour banner. The tour puts the starter's colour banner back.

00:52:41.627 --> 00:52:50.161
Colour. Six brand colours for the banner and the button: bay navy, paver red, lawn green, sand gold, slate and violet.

00:52:50.661 --> 00:52:57.461
Headline. The big words at the top, and a line under them (e.g. Reserve your spot before April).

00:52:57.961 --> 00:53:06.227
A picture in the message. An optional photo in the body, from a link or Upload. Once it's added, a Caption box appears.

00:53:06.727 --> 00:53:11.994
Who gets it. Choose the customers. The count at the bottom updates as you go.

00:53:12.494 --> 00:53:18.061
Customers or leads. Customers, Leads, Both, or Inactive customers.

00:53:18.561 --> 00:53:23.327
Residential or commercial. Any, Residential or Commercial.

00:53:23.827 --> 00:53:31.994
Towns. Click towns to send only there; none picked means everywhere. The number is how many customers each town has.

00:53:32.494 --> 00:53:43.127
Narrow it down. Had a kind of work in the last N months, lost an estimate lately, no work lately, on a maintenance plan or not. Demo customers stay out.

00:53:43.627 --> 00:53:52.361
How many get it. The count, a few names and a bar by town. Customers who opted out, or have no email, are never included.

00:53:52.861 --> 00:54:00.727
Send a test first. Type your email and press Send test to see it in a real inbox. It saves the draft first.

00:54:01.227 --> 00:54:06.894
Save draft. Keeps the campaign as a draft to finish later. The tour doesn't save.

00:54:07.394 --> 00:54:16.761
Send it. Sends to everyone counted, paced per hour (it asks first, and you can Stop it while it goes out). Greyed out until live email is on.

00:54:17.261 --> 00:54:23.861
What they'll see. A live preview with a sample customer's name, updated as you type and design.

00:54:24.361 --> 00:54:30.461
Back to campaigns. Leaves the composer. Nothing is kept unless you pressed Save draft.

00:54:30.811 --> 00:54:35.078
Design an email template with AI (or a ready layout).

00:54:35.778 --> 00:54:44.844
Design an email with AI. Opens the email designer. You describe the email and add photos; the design builds on the left.

00:54:45.344 --> 00:54:55.744
The email, live. Exactly what customers will get: the design, your words, and our footer with the unsubscribe line. Computer and Phone switch the width.

00:54:56.244 --> 00:55:08.711
Say what you want. What it's for, the feel, the colours and what to show. For example: a spring cleanup email for our regular customers, my patio photo across the top, fresh greens.

00:55:09.211 --> 00:55:14.378
Ideas to start from. Tap one to fill the box, then change it to suit.

00:55:14.878 --> 00:55:22.544
Attach your photos. Up to six photos of your work. Write what each one shows, so the design puts the right one on top.

00:55:23.044 --> 00:55:27.511
Main colour. Pick one of your colours, or let the design choose.

00:55:28.011 --> 00:55:44.511
Design it. The AI makes the design and its words. Then ask for any change, like a bigger headline; each change is a version you can go back to. AI has to be switched on for your account; until then, the ready layouts below do the same job.

00:55:45.011 --> 00:55:52.478
Or pick a ready layout. Four proven designs that take your photos, colour and words. Click Photo on top.

00:55:52.978 --> 00:56:03.211
The words. Subject, headline, the line under it, the message and the button. Every campaign made from this template starts with these, and can change them.

00:56:03.711 --> 00:56:08.078
Name it. A name you'll recognise, like Spring photo hero.

00:56:08.578 --> 00:56:17.511
Save as template. Keeps it in Email templates, ready for any campaign. The tour doesn't save anything: press it yourself when it's right.

00:56:17.861 --> 00:56:21.128
Use a saved email template in a campaign.

00:56:21.828 --> 00:56:29.428
Email templates. Every saved template, with a picture of it, who changed it last and how many campaigns use it.

00:56:29.928 --> 00:56:42.094
A template. Use in a campaign starts a new campaign with it. Edit opens it in the designer. The pen renames it; the bin deletes it, and campaigns already made with it keep their look.

00:56:42.561 --> 00:56:47.861
From any campaign. A campaign can also pick a template in its Design card.

00:56:48.361 --> 00:56:51.461
New campaign. Opens the composer.

00:56:51.961 --> 00:56:56.028
My templates. In the Design card, pick My templates.

00:56:56.528 --> 00:57:06.894
Pick one. Click a template's picture. The preview becomes the template with this campaign's own words, and you can still change the headline or the button colour here.

00:57:07.394 --> 00:57:14.094
What they'll see. The email exactly as customers get it, footer and unsubscribe line included.

00:57:14.444 --> 00:57:17.177
Spring / Fall cleanup sign-ups.

00:57:17.877 --> 00:57:22.911
Cleanup sign-ups. Your Spring and Fall forms and everyone who signed up.

00:57:23.411 --> 00:57:27.944
Your forms. See the form shows it exactly as customers see it.

00:57:28.444 --> 00:57:33.677
Someone calls instead. The same questions; they get their place in line.

00:57:34.177 --> 00:57:42.544
Work the list from #1. Accept books the visit or the stop-by quote; an auto-pay "call me" becomes a call for the office.

00:57:42.894 --> 00:57:45.594
Take a cleanup sign-up on the phone.

00:57:46.294 --> 00:57:50.061
Cleanup sign-ups. Phone sign-ups are taken here.

00:57:50.561 --> 00:57:55.827
Take a phone sign-up. On the season's card. The tour opens the Spring one.

00:57:56.327 --> 00:58:01.694
Who is calling. Name, phone and email. Name and phone are required.

00:58:02.194 --> 00:58:10.494
Where and when. The service address and town, and their preferred date or time frame (a range, now, a month, no preference).

00:58:10.994 --> 00:58:16.794
What they want. Tick the services from your form; Other is for anything not on the list.

00:58:17.294 --> 00:58:23.961
Estimate style. Meet a manager (an estimate visit is booked) or just send a quote (a stop-by to quote).

00:58:24.461 --> 00:58:32.294
Auto-pay call. Spring form: would they like a call about auto-pay? Yes turns into a separate call for the office.

00:58:32.794 --> 00:58:40.261
Billing changes and notes. A separate billing address or new contact details, and anything else they mention.

00:58:40.761 --> 00:58:47.194
Add to the list. Adds them in line with their number, like the online form. The tour doesn't save.

00:58:47.694 --> 00:58:52.161
Close the form. The x (or Cancel) closes it without saving.

00:58:52.661 --> 00:59:02.461
Work the list from #1. Accept books the estimate visit or the stop-by quote; the x dismisses. Requests are handled in the order received.

00:59:03.011 --> 00:59:13.982
Chapter seven. Jobs. Every job from won to paid: work items, permits, change orders, payments, job costing and the job folder.

00:59:14.182 --> 00:59:16.315
Everything on Jobs.

00:59:17.015 --> 00:59:26.882
Jobs. Every sold job, from "to schedule" to "paid". A job is made when an estimate is marked Won, with one work item per estimate section.

00:59:27.382 --> 00:59:33.515
Schedule board. Opens the crew board, where each piece of work gets its crew and its days.

00:59:34.015 --> 00:59:41.449
To schedule. Jobs with work that has no crew or start day yet. Click the box to list just those jobs.

00:59:41.949 --> 00:59:46.149
Scheduled. Jobs on the board, waiting for the crew to start.

00:59:46.649 --> 00:59:54.115
In progress. Jobs a crew has started (the crew lead presses Start on the phone, or the office does on the job).

00:59:54.615 --> 01:00:01.382
To invoice. Jobs whose work is all complete but not fully billed yet. Click the box to list them.

01:00:01.882 --> 01:00:10.849
Active jobs. The list opens on Active: sold, scheduled and in progress. The number on each tab is how many jobs are in it.

01:00:11.349 --> 01:00:17.749
To schedule tab. Jobs with work still to put on the board, approved change orders included.

01:00:18.249 --> 01:00:21.749
Complete. Finished jobs waiting to be invoiced.

01:00:22.249 --> 01:00:27.015
Invoiced / paid. Jobs that are billed, and the ones paid in full.

01:00:27.515 --> 01:00:30.515
All. Every job, whatever its status.

01:00:31.015 --> 01:00:39.749
Search the list. Type a job number, title, customer or town. The list filters as you type, inside the tab you are on.

01:00:40.249 --> 01:00:46.615
Job, customer, town. The job number and title, with the customer and the town under it.

01:00:47.115 --> 01:01:00.082
Status and flags. Sold, Scheduled, In progress, Complete, Invoiced or Paid. Tags: "1 to schedule" = work not on the board yet; a red Permit hold = it can't start yet.

01:01:00.582 --> 01:01:05.082
Crews. The crews doing the work, each with its colour from the board.

01:01:05.582 --> 01:01:09.849
When. The first and last day on the board, or "not scheduled".

01:01:10.349 --> 01:01:17.049
Work done. The ring shows work items complete out of the total: 1/3 means one of three is done.

01:01:17.549 --> 01:01:23.615
Value. The contract value. Only people who see money see this column and the next one.

01:01:24.115 --> 01:01:30.515
Paid so far. How much of the value is paid. The bar turns green when it is paid in full.

01:01:31.015 --> 01:01:42.582
Open a job. Click a row to open the job: work, crews, change orders, costs, payments and the folder. The list shows 50 at a time, with Previous / Next under it.

01:01:42.899 --> 01:01:45.066
Everything on a job.

01:01:45.766 --> 01:01:53.366
Open the job. Jobs open from the Jobs list, the Schedule board, the customer or search. Let's open one.

01:01:53.866 --> 01:02:03.666
The job at a glance. Job number, the estimate it came from, the title, address, phone and who sold it. The link above it goes back to the customer.

01:02:04.166 --> 01:02:11.066
Work order. Prints the crew's work order: the address, each work item, the crew notes and the materials.

01:02:11.566 --> 01:02:16.032
Schedule board. Opens the board on the week this job starts.

01:02:16.532 --> 01:02:27.666
Where the job is. Sold → Scheduled → In progress → Complete → Invoiced → Paid. It moves on by itself as work starts, finishes and is billed.

01:02:28.166 --> 01:02:40.132
Contract and signature. The contract number and whether it is signed. Mark signed records a paper signature (it asks first). Email signing link sends an online one when it is set up.

01:02:40.632 --> 01:02:48.099
Value, billed, paid. The contract plus approved change orders, what has been invoiced and what has been paid.

01:02:48.599 --> 01:03:01.699
Job costing. Is this job making money? Margin, profit so far, and estimate vs actual for hours, labor and materials. Tour: "Check a job's profit and enter its costs".

01:03:02.199 --> 01:03:13.166
Work. One work item per estimate section, each with its crew, hours and days. Schedule, Start and Complete are here. Tour: "Schedule, start and complete work".

01:03:13.666 --> 01:03:26.299
Change orders. Extra work the customer asks for, priced and signed on its own. Approved ones become work items and add to the job's value. Tour: "Price and approve a change order".

01:03:26.799 --> 01:03:36.466
Costs. Material bills, vendor invoices, subcontractors, equipment, dump fees and permits bought for this job. They feed the profit above.

01:03:36.966 --> 01:03:45.632
Crew time. Each person's hours on this job, day by day: time on site plus their share of the yard, loading and travel time.

01:03:46.132 --> 01:03:53.932
From the crew. What the crew lead's phone recorded: start and finish with the time, photos and how far they were from the address.

01:03:54.432 --> 01:04:03.299
Job timeline. Everything that happened on the job, newest first: scheduled, moved, started, change orders, invoices, payments.

01:04:03.799 --> 01:04:13.366
Payments. The payment schedule: invoice each step in one click, see what is paid and what is due next. Tour: "Invoice a job's payment schedule".

01:04:13.832 --> 01:04:24.566
Job folder. The paper cover sheet, ticked by itself as things happen: start date, contract emailed and signed, payments, permit, final bill, inspection.

01:04:25.066 --> 01:04:36.232
Contract terms. The payment schedule in words, the NJ ST-8 for a capital improvement (no sales tax), and whether the customer gets "you're on the schedule" emails.

01:04:36.732 --> 01:04:46.899
Working days. Long jobs skip weekends unless you switch Saturdays or Sundays on for this job. Tour: "Keep the job folder, permit and terms".

01:04:47.366 --> 01:05:00.532
Cards that come and go. Only when they apply: a red Permit hold banner, Maintenance plan, Bill tracked time, Material selections, Customer survey. Help lists a tour for each part of the job.

01:05:00.849 --> 01:05:04.249
Schedule, start and complete work on a job.

01:05:04.949 --> 01:05:09.649
Open the job. Work items live on the job. Let's open one.

01:05:10.149 --> 01:05:18.416
Work items. One item per estimate section and per approved change order, each with its own crew, crew-hours and days.

01:05:18.916 --> 01:05:22.782
Add work. For extra work that is not on the estimate.

01:05:23.282 --> 01:05:27.349
What. Say what the work is, e.g. Extra steps.

01:05:27.849 --> 01:05:35.016
Crew-hours. The hours the crew needs in total. The board turns them into days using the crew's hours a day.

01:05:35.516 --> 01:05:40.082
Crew. Who does it. You can leave it and pick the crew when you schedule it.

01:05:40.582 --> 01:05:46.949
Add it. Add puts it on the job and in the "To schedule" list on the board. The tour doesn't press it.

01:05:47.449 --> 01:05:52.116
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:05:52.616 --> 01:06:01.149
One work item. Crew colour, the name, work order number, crew, crew-hours, hours the crew logged and photos, then its status.

01:06:01.649 --> 01:06:10.516
Its days. The days it is booked. A red "over" day means the crew has more hours than it can do that day: move this or the other work.

01:06:11.016 --> 01:06:16.482
Reopen. On a finished item: puts it back in progress when the crew has to go back.

01:06:16.982 --> 01:06:26.516
Complete. Marks the item done. When the last item is done the job turns Complete, ready to invoice. The crew lead can also do it on the phone.

01:06:27.016 --> 01:06:33.182
Materials. Click Materials to see what this item needs. A tick means the crew loaded it.

01:06:33.682 --> 01:06:41.149
Reschedule. Opens the schedule form for this item. On an item not on the board yet the button says Schedule.

01:06:41.649 --> 01:06:45.249
Crew. Pick the crew; each shows its speciality.

01:06:45.749 --> 01:06:48.516
Start day. The first day on site.

01:06:49.016 --> 01:06:56.282
Budgeted crew-hours. The hours budgeted. The days are these hours ÷ the crew's hours a day.

01:06:56.782 --> 01:07:03.216
Or set the days. Leave 0 to work the days out from the hours, or type the number of days.

01:07:03.716 --> 01:07:11.082
The days it takes. A preview of the days. Weekends are skipped unless the job works them (Working days card).

01:07:11.582 --> 01:07:16.016
Take it off the board. Puts the item back in the To schedule list.

01:07:16.516 --> 01:07:24.282
Book the days. Schedule books it and tells you if the crew goes over capacity on any day. The tour doesn't press it.

01:07:24.782 --> 01:07:29.449
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:07:29.949 --> 01:07:37.516
Not on the board yet. An item with no days says "Not on the schedule yet" and has a Schedule button: the same form.

01:07:38.016 --> 01:07:45.449
Remove an item. The bin removes an item that has not started (it asks first). It comes off the schedule too.

01:07:45.949 --> 01:07:52.682
Crew note. A note for the crew on this item, from the estimate or a change order. It shows on their phone.

01:07:53.182 --> 01:07:58.449
Open the job. Now a job that is booked but not started, to see Start.

01:07:58.949 --> 01:08:08.649
Start. Marks the item in progress (the crew lead usually does it on the phone). A job on Permit hold shows a red tag instead and can't start.

01:08:08.999 --> 01:08:12.366
Permits: no start before the township approves.

01:08:13.066 --> 01:08:16.599
Open a job. Permits are kept on the job.

01:08:17.099 --> 01:08:29.432
The job folder. Tick "Needs a township permit" and fill in the township and dates. The crew can't start until you press "Mark the permit approved"; the job shows a lock on the schedule meanwhile.

01:08:29.782 --> 01:08:32.515
Price and approve a change order.

01:08:33.215 --> 01:08:38.015
Open the job. Change orders live on the job. Let's open one.

01:08:38.515 --> 01:08:47.349
Change orders. Extra work the customer asks for, each priced and signed on its own and kept apart from the original contract.

01:08:47.849 --> 01:08:56.582
Start one. New change order starts a draft on this job straight away (CO-1, CO-2 …), ready to fill in. The tour doesn't press it.

01:08:57.082 --> 01:09:07.449
An approved one. The stamp shows its state: Draft, With customer, Approved or Declined. Then the lines, crew-hours, who approved it and how it is billed.

01:09:07.949 --> 01:09:14.949
Print it. Prints the approved change order. If it was billed on its own invoice, a button opens that invoice.

01:09:15.449 --> 01:09:22.982
A draft. A draft, or one with the customer, can still change: Edit, Print, Approved, and the x for declined.

01:09:23.482 --> 01:09:26.282
Edit. Opens it to write the lines.

01:09:26.782 --> 01:09:32.449
Title. A short name the customer understands, e.g. Patio extension.

01:09:32.949 --> 01:09:39.249
Estimated crew-hours. Becomes the crew's hour budget on the work item once it is approved.

01:09:39.749 --> 01:09:50.582
The lines. What changes, quantity, price, your cost (never shown to the customer) and the Tax tick. The x removes a line; the total before tax is under it.

01:09:51.082 --> 01:09:53.882
Add a line. Adds another line.

01:09:54.382 --> 01:10:01.549
Save it. Saves the lines. Tax follows the job (none on an ST-8 job). The tour doesn't press it.

01:10:02.049 --> 01:10:05.815
Close without saving. Cancel closes the editor.

01:10:06.315 --> 01:10:10.715
Give it to the customer. Print prints it and marks it "With customer".

01:10:11.215 --> 01:10:22.582
The customer agreed. Approved asks who approved it and how to bill it: with the final invoice, now on its own invoice, in the final payment or spread over the payments left.

01:10:23.082 --> 01:10:30.582
The customer said no. Marks it Declined (it asks first). It stays on the job; a declined one can be deleted.

01:10:31.082 --> 01:10:43.049
It becomes work. Once approved it is a CO work item with its own hours, scheduled like any other work. Its price adds to the job. You can attach the signed copy when approving.

01:10:43.399 --> 01:10:46.266
Invoice a job's payment schedule.

01:10:46.966 --> 01:10:52.032
Open the job. The payment schedule is on the job. Let's open one.

01:10:52.532 --> 01:10:59.132
Payments. The payment schedule from the contract. Invoice each payment in one click when it is due.

01:10:59.632 --> 01:11:06.699
The totals. Contract (with change orders), invoiced, paid and remaining, then the next payment due and when.

01:11:07.199 --> 01:11:15.166
Each payment. A tick once paid, then the name, the %, when it is due, Invoiced or Not invoiced yet, and the amount.

01:11:15.632 --> 01:11:22.732
Open its invoice. Once a payment is invoiced, this opens the invoice to send it or record a payment.

01:11:23.232 --> 01:11:33.632
Invoice a payment. Makes a draft invoice for that payment and opens it to check and send. Once the job is complete, "Invoice the balance" bills what is left.

01:11:34.132 --> 01:11:40.266
Change the schedule. Edit schedule re-plans the payments still to bill (owner and office).

01:11:40.766 --> 01:11:48.199
Invoiced ones are locked. Payments already invoiced stay as they are. The ones below share what is still to bill.

01:11:48.699 --> 01:11:53.832
Start from a preset. One click fills a common schedule; then adjust it.

01:11:54.332 --> 01:12:04.266
One payment. Its name; the arrows move it up or down and x removes it. Then % of the rest, a fixed $ or the balance, and when it is due.

01:12:04.766 --> 01:12:07.832
Add a payment. Adds another payment.

01:12:08.332 --> 01:12:13.532
Save it. Checks it adds up to what is left, then saves. The tour doesn't press it.

01:12:14.032 --> 01:12:17.799
Leave it as it was. Cancel closes the editor.

01:12:18.299 --> 01:12:24.666
Invoices on this job. Every invoice for this job with its status. Click one to open it.

01:12:25.166 --> 01:12:32.032
Also in the job folder. The folder lists each payment again with how it was paid, for the paper file.

01:12:32.382 --> 01:12:35.715
Check a job's profit and enter its costs.

01:12:36.415 --> 01:12:41.382
Open the job. Profit and costs are on the job. Let's open one.

01:12:41.882 --> 01:12:51.649
Job costing. Running numbers while the job is on, final numbers once it is complete. They move as the crew logs time and costs come in.

01:12:52.149 --> 01:13:05.149
Margin and profit. The ring is the margin. Beside it: gross profit so far (or the estimated profit before work starts), the revenue with change orders, and the estimated margin.

01:13:05.649 --> 01:13:16.782
Where the money goes. The top bar is actual: labor, materials, subs, other, and what is left as profit. The bar under it is the estimate. The colour key is below.

01:13:17.282 --> 01:13:28.849
Estimate vs actual. Crew hours, labor, materials, subcontractors, other and total cost: estimated, actual and the difference (red = over the estimate).

01:13:29.315 --> 01:13:36.315
By work item. Opens the same comparison for each work item; change orders are marked CO.

01:13:36.815 --> 01:13:46.049
Profit report. Opens Reports → Job costing with every job side by side. The burn rates that price labor are set there.

01:13:46.549 --> 01:13:52.849
Costs. Everything bought for this job. Add bills as they come in and the profit above updates.

01:13:53.349 --> 01:13:56.415
Add a cost. Opens the cost form.

01:13:56.915 --> 01:14:02.782
Kind. Materials, Subcontractor, Equipment, Dump / disposal, Permit or Other.

01:14:03.282 --> 01:14:08.182
Vendor. Who you paid, e.g. Cedar Bridge Landscape Supply.

01:14:08.682 --> 01:14:13.149
Amount. What it cost. A credit can go in as a minus amount.

01:14:13.649 --> 01:14:21.915
Their invoice # and date. The vendor's invoice number (you are warned if it is on this job twice) and the date beside it.

01:14:22.415 --> 01:14:29.282
For (optional). Leave it on the whole job, or charge it to one work item or an approved change order.

01:14:29.782 --> 01:14:36.049
Description. What it was, e.g. 12 pallets Techo-Bloc, 4 t stone dust.

01:14:36.549 --> 01:14:40.982
Attach receipt. Attach a photo or PDF of the bill.

01:14:41.482 --> 01:14:46.849
Save the cost. Add cost saves it against the job. The tour doesn't press it.

01:14:47.349 --> 01:14:52.015
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:14:52.515 --> 01:14:56.515
Change a cost. The pencil opens a cost to correct it.

01:14:57.015 --> 01:15:01.782
Remove a cost. The bin takes it off the job's costs (it asks first).

01:15:02.282 --> 01:15:10.715
Crew time by person. Each day, each person: hours on site + their share of yard and travel time, and what it cost.

01:15:11.065 --> 01:15:14.232
Keep the job folder, permit and terms.

01:15:14.932 --> 01:15:19.332
Open the job. The folder is on the job. Let's open one.

01:15:19.832 --> 01:15:28.932
The job folder. The paper cover sheet, kept up to date by itself from the contract, payments and invoices. You tick the rest here.

01:15:29.432 --> 01:15:39.632
Filled in by itself. Start date, contract emailed, signed contract, the ST-8, each payment and the final bill tick themselves as they happen.

01:15:40.132 --> 01:15:47.565
Ticked by you. Account tagged, the permit and the final inspection are filled in with the pencil (Edit the folder).

01:15:48.065 --> 01:15:56.465
Contract and payments. The contract plus change orders, then each payment: paid (and how), part paid or not paid yet.

01:15:56.965 --> 01:16:01.565
Print the cover sheet. Prints it like the paper one, for the job file.

01:16:02.065 --> 01:16:06.032
Edit the folder. Dates the system can't know go in here.

01:16:06.532 --> 01:16:10.098
Account tagged. Tick it once the account is tagged.

01:16:10.598 --> 01:16:20.865
Permit needed. Then the job can't start until the permit is approved: a red Permit hold banner on the job (Mark the permit approved) and a lock on the board.

01:16:21.365 --> 01:16:32.165
Time and materials. Bills the crew's on-site man-hours. A "Bill tracked time" card then shows: enter the rate per man-hour, then Make the invoice (a line per day).

01:16:32.665 --> 01:16:40.098
Emailed contract on. Blank = the day the estimate went out. Type a date if the contract went another day.

01:16:40.598 --> 01:16:43.798
Permit #. The township's permit number.

01:16:44.298 --> 01:16:50.598
Permit fee. Goes on the final invoice, or press Bill now on the folder to bill it on its own.

01:16:51.098 --> 01:16:58.632
Permit status. To apply for, Applied, Approved, Inspection booked, Passed, Failed inspection or Not needed.

01:16:59.132 --> 01:17:04.298
Municipality. Long Beach Twp, Stafford, Ship Bottom …

01:17:04.798 --> 01:17:09.832
Permit dates. Applied for on, Approved on, and the next inspection.

01:17:10.332 --> 01:17:14.698
Inspection notes. What the inspector said, or what is booked.

01:17:15.198 --> 01:17:24.532
Final inspection. Its date and your initials. A complete permit job without one shows "Call for the final inspection" on the folder.

01:17:25.032 --> 01:17:27.798
Notes. Anything else for the folder.

01:17:28.298 --> 01:17:32.765
Save the folder. Save folder keeps it. The tour doesn't press it.

01:17:33.265 --> 01:17:37.932
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:17:38.432 --> 01:17:50.665
Contract terms. The payment schedule in words. On a capital improvement an ST-8 box shows: no sales tax, so upload the customer's signed NJ ST-8 there.

01:17:51.165 --> 01:18:03.232
Tell the customer their date. Auto follows the type of work. On or Off sets it for this job: On sends a "you're on the schedule" email when the date is set or moves. It saves at once.

01:18:03.732 --> 01:18:11.698
Work weekends?. Switch on Saturdays or Sundays for this job. It saves at once and the scheduled days move to match.

01:18:12.049 --> 01:18:15.249
See a job's maintenance plan and survey.

01:18:15.949 --> 01:18:22.216
Open the job. A maintenance plan keeps its visits on a job of its own. Let's open one.

01:18:22.716 --> 01:18:31.916
Maintenance plan. The plan's number, service and how often. Each visit is a work item on this job. Open goes to the Maintenance screen.

01:18:32.416 --> 01:18:38.882
One item per visit. The plan books each visit; Reschedule or Start it like any other work.

01:18:39.382 --> 01:18:42.382
Finished jobs. Now a finished job.

01:18:42.882 --> 01:18:46.949
Open the job. The survey shows once a job is done.

01:18:47.449 --> 01:18:56.216
Customer survey. After the job the customer gets a survey. Their score shows here; 3 or less opens a ticket to call them.

01:18:56.716 --> 01:19:08.616
Material selections. When the estimate has the customer's picks, a Material selections card shows above Working days: approved or not, Selection sheet and Print / PDF.

01:19:09.165 --> 01:19:17.981
Chapter eight. Schedule. Crews down the side, days across: scheduling, moving work for rain, and the warnings.

01:19:18.181 --> 01:19:20.414
Everything on the Schedule.

01:19:21.114 --> 01:19:30.048
The Schedule board. Crews down the side, days across, two weeks at a time. Every sold piece of work gets its crew and its days here.

01:19:30.548 --> 01:19:36.481
Move through the weeks. The arrows go back or forward a week; Today comes back to this week.

01:19:36.981 --> 01:19:44.014
Board or month. Crews · 2 weeks is this board; Month shows the whole month. We'll look at Month at the end.

01:19:44.514 --> 01:19:51.881
To schedule. Every sold piece of work without a crew and a start day waits here, approved change orders too.

01:19:52.381 --> 01:20:03.448
Waiting work. Job colour, work name, customer, job number, town, crew-hours and when it was sold. A red Permit hold tag: it can be booked but can't start yet.

01:20:03.948 --> 01:20:08.514
Schedule it from here. The calendar button opens the schedule form.

01:20:09.014 --> 01:20:11.048
Crew. Pick the crew.

01:20:11.614 --> 01:20:14.114
Start. The first day on site.

01:20:14.614 --> 01:20:23.014
Budgeted crew-hours. Days = these hours ÷ the crew's hours a day. A preview of the days shows under the form.

01:20:23.514 --> 01:20:28.481
Days. Or type the number of days yourself (0 = from the hours).

01:20:28.981 --> 01:20:36.114
Book it. Schedule books it and tells you if the crew goes over capacity on any day. The tour doesn't press it.

01:20:36.614 --> 01:20:41.281
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:20:41.781 --> 01:20:49.381
Or drag it. Drag a card onto a crew's start day and the form opens there. Or click the card to pick it, like this …

01:20:49.881 --> 01:20:56.614
… then click the day. … then click the crew's start day on the board: the form opens with that crew and day.

01:20:57.114 --> 01:21:00.881
Put it back. Click the picked card again to let go of it.

01:21:01.381 --> 01:21:07.981
Appointments row. How many sales visits and tasks there are each day, and whose. Hover for the times.

01:21:08.481 --> 01:21:13.781
A crew. Crew colour, name, lead and how many crew-hours it can do in a day.

01:21:14.281 --> 01:21:26.848
Booked work. One colour per job, the same every day it runs (↳ = continues). Click it to open the job; drag it to another day or crew to move it. A multi-day job moves together.

01:21:27.348 --> 01:21:36.848
How full the day is. The line under a day is the crew's load against what it can do. Faded blocks are done; work that has started can't be dragged.

01:21:37.348 --> 01:21:46.048
Over capacity. A red outline: the crew is booked for more hours than it can do that day. Move something to another day or crew.

01:21:46.548 --> 01:21:58.148
What the colours mean. Bars: one colour per job, faded = done. Each crew's colour and hours a day, the red over-capacity outline, and the lock for a permit hold.

01:21:58.648 --> 01:22:01.314
Month view. Shows the whole month.

01:22:01.814 --> 01:22:09.381
The month. Here a colour is a crew (the key is above). Click a bar to open the job; drag it to another day to move it.

01:22:09.848 --> 01:22:14.881
Other months. The arrows go a month back or forward; This month comes back.

01:22:15.381 --> 01:22:19.748
Back to the board. Crews · 2 weeks goes back to the crew board.

01:22:20.098 --> 01:22:23.831
Schedule work, assign crews, move it (rain days).

01:22:24.531 --> 01:22:31.198
Waiting to be scheduled. Every sold piece of work waits here until it has a crew and a start day.

01:22:31.698 --> 01:22:40.998
Drag it onto a crew. Drag it onto a crew's start day (or click it, then the day). The days come from the crew-hours ÷ the crew size.

01:22:41.498 --> 01:22:50.265
Move it any time. Drag a block to another day or crew; a multi-day job moves together. A lock means it waits on a permit.

01:22:50.765 --> 01:22:54.098
Month view. The whole month, coloured by crew.

01:22:54.598 --> 01:23:00.731
What the colours mean. Each job its own colour on the board; each crew its own colour in the month.

01:23:01.281 --> 01:23:08.753
Chapter nine. Maintenance. Maintenance plans and their visits, and the yearly price change.

01:23:08.953 --> 01:23:11.253
Everything on Maintenance.

01:23:11.953 --> 01:23:21.753
Maintenance. Recurring work: lawn care, beds, spring and fall cleanups, snow. Plans put their own visits on the crew's schedule weeks ahead.

01:23:22.253 --> 01:23:30.486
The numbers. Active plans and visits this week. People who see money also see the yearly value and what is ready to bill.

01:23:30.986 --> 01:23:40.920
Yearly increase. Owner and office: raise every plan's price from a date and email each customer. Tour: "Raise maintenance prices for the year".

01:23:41.420 --> 01:23:45.320
New plan. Starts a plan; first pick the customer.

01:23:45.820 --> 01:23:54.920
Find the customer. Type a name, phone or street and click them; the plan form opens. Tour: "Set up or change a maintenance plan".

01:23:55.420 --> 01:23:59.620
Close the form. The x closes it without starting a plan.

01:24:00.120 --> 01:24:06.486
Plans. Every plan; the number on each tab is how many. Visits and Billing are next to it.

01:24:06.986 --> 01:24:10.053
Customer. Who the plan is for, and where.

01:24:10.553 --> 01:24:19.320
Service and how often. Weekly, every 2 weeks, monthly, quarterly, spring + fall or snow (on call), and the day of the week.

01:24:19.820 --> 01:24:26.886
Season. The months it runs are green; the mark is this month. Visits only go on the schedule in season.

01:24:27.386 --> 01:24:32.320
Crew. The crew that does the visits. With No crew, no visits get booked.

01:24:32.820 --> 01:24:37.586
Price. Per visit, a month (fixed monthly fee), or not billed here.

01:24:38.086 --> 01:24:45.053
Next visit. The next booked visit and how many are done this year, or on call, needs a crew, out of season.

01:24:45.553 --> 01:24:48.720
Status. Active, Paused or Ended.

01:24:49.220 --> 01:24:54.986
Open a plan. Click a plan to change it, move or skip a visit, pause or end it.

01:24:55.486 --> 01:24:58.720
Visits. This week and next, day by day.

01:24:59.220 --> 01:25:06.620
The visit board. Each visit is coloured by its crew; faded = done. Click a visit to open the customer.

01:25:07.120 --> 01:25:10.186
Billing. Month-end billing for maintenance.

01:25:10.686 --> 01:25:16.986
Bill up to. Finished visits and monthly fees up to this date. Change it and the list updates.

01:25:17.486 --> 01:25:25.820
Who gets billed. One draft invoice per customer: a line per finished visit, or the monthly fee for each month in season.

01:25:26.320 --> 01:25:33.620
Make the invoices. Creates the draft invoices; check and send them from Invoices. The tour doesn't press it.

01:25:34.120 --> 01:25:38.120
Back to the plans. Plans is where most of the work is.

01:25:38.470 --> 01:25:41.337
Set up or change a maintenance plan.

01:25:42.037 --> 01:25:47.703
New plan. Starts a plan for a customer (a customer's page can start one too).

01:25:48.203 --> 01:25:54.770
Pick the customer. Type a name, phone or street and click the customer; the plan form opens.

01:25:55.270 --> 01:25:59.470
Close the form. The x closes it without starting a plan.

01:25:59.970 --> 01:26:05.503
Open a plan. An existing plan opens in the same form. Let's open one.

01:26:06.003 --> 01:26:10.270
Service. What the plan is, e.g. Weekly lawn care.

01:26:10.770 --> 01:26:16.470
From the catalogue. Click a catalogue item to fill in the service name and its price.

01:26:16.970 --> 01:26:27.337
How often. Weekly, every 2 weeks, monthly, quarterly, spring + fall, or Snow (on call: add a visit when it snows; pricing is on the Snow screen).

01:26:27.837 --> 01:26:30.437
Crew. The crew that does the visits.

01:26:30.937 --> 01:26:34.837
Day of the week. The day the visits fall on, or Any.

01:26:35.337 --> 01:26:42.137
Season. Season from and to; the strip under it shows the months. No visits outside the season.

01:26:42.637 --> 01:26:47.337
Start and end. When the plan starts, and an end date if it has one.

01:26:47.837 --> 01:26:53.637
Crew-hours a visit. How long a visit takes. It counts against the crew's day on the board.

01:26:54.137 --> 01:26:57.703
Price. The price per visit, or the monthly fee.

01:26:58.203 --> 01:27:04.837
Billing. Each finished visit (billed at month end), a fixed monthly fee in season, or not billed here.

01:27:05.337 --> 01:27:10.770
Note for the crew. Gate code, dog, what to skip … It shows on the crew's phone.

01:27:11.270 --> 01:27:19.170
Tell the customer. Emails the customer the date of the first visit. Handy for cleanups; leave it off for weekly mowing.

01:27:19.670 --> 01:27:25.437
Next visits. The next dates the plan will book. They change as you change the settings.

01:27:25.937 --> 01:27:29.303
Booked visits. Visits already on the schedule.

01:27:29.770 --> 01:27:34.137
Move a visit. Move puts a visit on another day (a rain day).

01:27:34.637 --> 01:27:39.770
Skip a visit. Skip drops that visit; it stays skipped and won't come back.

01:27:40.270 --> 01:27:46.803
Save the plan. Save plan (Create plan for a new one) books its visits. The tour doesn't press it.

01:27:47.303 --> 01:27:52.370
Pause. Pause takes the future visits off; Resume brings the plan back.

01:27:52.870 --> 01:27:59.837
End the plan. Future visits come off the schedule; finished visits can still be billed. It asks first.

01:28:00.337 --> 01:28:05.003
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:28:05.353 --> 01:28:08.253
Raise maintenance prices for the year.

01:28:08.953 --> 01:28:14.453
Yearly increase. Raises every maintenance plan due its increase, in one go.

01:28:14.953 --> 01:28:21.753
Increase. The % to add. Leave it blank to use each plan's own % (5% unless set).

01:28:22.253 --> 01:28:26.820
Starting. From this date visits not billed yet take the new price.

01:28:27.320 --> 01:28:32.786
Tell the customers. Emails each customer who has an email their new price.

01:28:33.286 --> 01:28:42.420
Which plans. Each plan due: last increase, price now, new price, %. Untick any to skip. Per-storm snow plans are left out.

01:28:42.920 --> 01:28:50.286
Apply it. Apply the increase shows the yearly value before and after and asks first. The tour doesn't press it.

01:28:50.786 --> 01:28:55.453
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:28:56.003 --> 01:29:04.286
Chapter ten. Deliveries. Material deliveries and the container yard: drops, pickups and swaps.

01:29:04.486 --> 01:29:06.719
Everything on Deliveries.

01:29:07.419 --> 01:29:15.486
Deliveries. The drivers' week (instead of the Google Calendar and the whiteboard) and every dumpster: where it is and who has it.

01:29:15.953 --> 01:29:19.519
Pick the week. The arrows go back or forward a week.

01:29:20.019 --> 01:29:28.786
New run. Books a material delivery, or a container drop, pickup, swap or move. Tour: "Book a delivery or container run".

01:29:29.286 --> 01:29:34.086
Runs today. Runs still to do today, and which drivers have them.

01:29:34.586 --> 01:29:38.419
This week. All the runs this week and how many are done.

01:29:38.919 --> 01:29:44.653
Containers out. Containers at customers, out of all of them; the rest are in the yard.

01:29:45.153 --> 01:29:56.553
Full or late. Containers the customer says are full, waiting for pickup. With none, it counts late runs: earlier days not done, also listed in a red banner.

01:29:57.053 --> 01:30:06.586
The drivers' week. A row per driver, a column per day (Sunday only when a run is on it). Not assigned holds runs with no driver yet.

01:30:07.086 --> 01:30:16.653
A run. Time, container number, customer, and what it is with the truck. The edge colour is the kind of run; done runs are faded with a tick.

01:30:17.153 --> 01:30:25.119
Drag to move. Drag a run to another day or driver to move it; the driver's phone follows. Done runs stay put.

01:30:25.586 --> 01:30:30.853
Add a run on a day. The + in a day starts a run for that driver and day.

01:30:31.353 --> 01:30:34.719
Open a run. Click a run to see all of it.

01:30:35.186 --> 01:30:43.653
The details. What, when, driver, truck, customer, address, container, job, load and notes; once done, who did it and when.

01:30:44.153 --> 01:30:47.886
Edit. Changes the run (the same form as New run).

01:30:48.386 --> 01:30:56.353
Mark done. For when the driver couldn't on the phone. A drop asks which container went out; the container moves with the run.

01:30:56.853 --> 01:31:00.419
Cancel run. Cancels the run (it asks first).

01:31:00.919 --> 01:31:03.586
Customer. Opens the customer.

01:31:04.086 --> 01:31:08.753
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:31:09.253 --> 01:31:17.153
Container yard. Every dumpster / roll-off: its number, size, where it is and what's next. Tour: "Track dumpsters".

01:31:17.653 --> 01:31:21.286
Out. Containers at customers, full ones too.

01:31:21.786 --> 01:31:23.953
Yard. Ready to go.

01:31:24.453 --> 01:31:26.686
Repair. Out of service.

01:31:27.186 --> 01:31:29.419
All. Back to all of them.

01:31:29.953 --> 01:31:34.519
Add container. A new dumpster: its number, size and notes.

01:31:35.019 --> 01:31:46.353
A container. Size, number, status (In the yard, Out, Full · pickup due, Repair), customer and address, days out and the next run. Click it for history and actions.

01:31:46.703 --> 01:31:49.636
Book a delivery or container run.

01:31:50.336 --> 01:31:53.136
New run. Opens the run form.

01:31:53.636 --> 01:32:01.703
What kind of run. Material delivery, drop a container, pick one up, swap (dump and bring it back), move one, or any other run.

01:32:02.203 --> 01:32:04.436
Day. The day of the run.

01:32:04.970 --> 01:32:07.203
Time. The start time.

01:32:07.703 --> 01:32:12.470
Takes. How long it keeps the driver busy: 30 minutes up to all day.

01:32:12.970 --> 01:32:18.903
Driver. Only drivers are listed. Leave it empty and the run goes under Not assigned.

01:32:19.403 --> 01:32:25.803
Customer. Search by name, phone or street and pick them from the list; the address becomes theirs.

01:32:26.303 --> 01:32:32.270
Address. Only if it is not the customer's address: a job site, a second property …

01:32:32.770 --> 01:32:38.836
A container run. For a drop, pickup, swap or move the form asks which container.

01:32:39.336 --> 01:32:47.736
Container. For a drop: one from the yard, or leave it for the driver. For a pickup, swap or move: the one at the customer.

01:32:48.236 --> 01:32:50.636
Truck. Which truck (from Fleet).

01:32:51.136 --> 01:32:59.570
Load / what for. For a delivery, the load (6 pallets pavers, 22 t QP). For a container, what it is for.

01:33:00.070 --> 01:33:05.503
Notes for the driver. Gate code, where to put it … The driver sees it on the phone.

01:33:06.003 --> 01:33:15.436
Book it. Schedule run saves it and the driver sees it on the phone. You are warned if the truck or container is busy. The tour doesn't press it.

01:33:15.936 --> 01:33:20.603
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:33:21.103 --> 01:33:27.903
Quicker: + on a day. The + in a driver's day opens the same form for that day and driver.

01:33:28.403 --> 01:33:37.970
From a container. A container's card books runs too: Schedule pickup or Swap for one that is out, Drop it at a customer for one in the yard.

01:33:38.320 --> 01:33:41.587
Track dumpsters: drop, pick up, swap.

01:33:42.253 --> 01:33:47.487
Container yard. Every dumpster / roll-off, where it is and what is next.

01:33:47.987 --> 01:33:52.453
Filter. All, Out, Yard or Repair, with how many are in each.

01:33:52.953 --> 01:33:56.020
Add container. Adds a new dumpster.

01:33:56.520 --> 01:34:00.453
Number. Its own number, e.g. D-18.

01:34:00.953 --> 01:34:05.320
Size. 10, 15, 20, 30 or 40 yards.

01:34:05.820 --> 01:34:08.687
Notes. Anything worth knowing about it.

01:34:09.187 --> 01:34:13.453
Save it. Save adds it to the yard. The tour doesn't press it.

01:34:13.953 --> 01:34:18.620
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:34:19.120 --> 01:34:23.420
One that is out. Click it to see where it is and what it has done.

01:34:23.920 --> 01:34:31.187
Where it is. Status, size, customer, address, job, out since (and how many days) and the next run.

01:34:31.687 --> 01:34:36.853
History. Every drop, pickup, swap, move and repair, with who and when.

01:34:37.353 --> 01:34:42.620
Schedule pickup. Books a pickup run with the customer and address filled in.

01:34:43.120 --> 01:34:46.487
Swap. Books a swap: dump it and bring it back.

01:34:46.987 --> 01:34:52.953
Customer says full. Marks it Full · pickup due; it shows on the Full box at the top.

01:34:53.453 --> 01:35:00.053
Edit. Change the number, size or notes. Owner and office can remove one that is in the yard.

01:35:00.553 --> 01:35:05.220
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:35:05.720 --> 01:35:08.387
One in the yard. Ready to go.

01:35:08.887 --> 01:35:13.220
Drop it at a customer. Books a drop run with this container.

01:35:13.720 --> 01:35:16.720
Needs repair. Takes it out of service.

01:35:17.220 --> 01:35:21.887
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:35:22.387 --> 01:35:25.053
One in repair. Out of service.

01:35:25.553 --> 01:35:29.520
Back in service. Puts it back in the yard, ready to go.

01:35:30.020 --> 01:35:34.687
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:35:35.187 --> 01:35:41.287
Full · pickup due. The customer says it is full. Book its pickup or a swap from its card.

01:35:41.836 --> 01:35:49.436
Chapter eleven. Snow. Snow sites, their pricing, the crews' logs and billing the storm.

01:35:49.636 --> 01:35:51.669
Everything on Snow.

01:35:52.369 --> 01:35:59.069
Snow. The snow log and snow billing: how many properties, visits logged and what is ready to bill.

01:35:59.569 --> 01:36:05.703
Log a visit. For a visit the crew didn't log on the phone, or from the paper snow log.

01:36:06.203 --> 01:36:09.403
Property. The property, from its snow plan.

01:36:09.903 --> 01:36:12.236
Date. The day of the visit.

01:36:12.736 --> 01:36:19.503
Storm. Name the storm to group its visits (e.g. February 8 storm). Blank groups them by date.

01:36:20.003 --> 01:36:25.736
Snowfall. Inches at the property. Snowfall pricing uses the biggest per storm.

01:36:26.236 --> 01:36:32.803
Time in and out. When the crew arrived and left, and how many men; hourly pricing uses them.

01:36:33.303 --> 01:36:37.869
Truck, driver, crew. Which plow truck, who drove, and the crew.

01:36:38.369 --> 01:36:43.036
What was done. Plowed the lot, Salted, Shoveled walks, Calcium.

01:36:43.536 --> 01:36:49.469
Salt, ice melt, loader. How much salt and ice melt went down, and the loader hours.

01:36:49.969 --> 01:36:55.803
Site condition. How it was left, e.g. Clear · icy spots by the door.

01:36:56.303 --> 01:37:01.469
Save the visit. Log visit saves it to the log. The tour doesn't press it.

01:37:01.969 --> 01:37:06.636
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:37:07.136 --> 01:37:16.636
Bill snow. One draft invoice per customer for every unbilled visit on a priced plan (it asks first). Check and send them from Invoices.

01:37:17.136 --> 01:37:25.269
A storm. Visits grouped by storm: the date, how many properties and visits, billed or not, and the biggest snowfall.

01:37:25.769 --> 01:37:34.869
A visit. Property, times, hours, men, truck, driver, whether it came from the crew app, the site condition, what was done, and any photos.

01:37:35.369 --> 01:37:39.336
Change a visit. Opens the visit in the same form.

01:37:39.836 --> 01:37:47.303
Remove a visit. Removes it (it asks first). A billed visit shows its invoice number instead and can't change.

01:37:47.803 --> 01:37:54.936
Snow plans. One plan per property, made on Maintenance (how often: Snow). New plan takes you there.

01:37:55.436 --> 01:38:03.403
Visits to bill. Logged visits on that property not billed yet. A yellow banner warns when a plan has no pricing.

01:38:03.903 --> 01:38:11.836
Pricing. How the property is billed: by snowfall or by the hour. Tour: "Price snow by snowfall or by the hour".

01:38:12.336 --> 01:38:17.136
To bill. Each customer's total ready to bill, priced from their plan.

01:38:17.636 --> 01:38:22.469
See the lines. Click a customer to see each visit's line and price.

01:38:22.820 --> 01:38:25.987
Price snow by snowfall or by the hour.

01:38:26.687 --> 01:38:30.453
Open the pricing. The $ next to a snow plan.

01:38:30.953 --> 01:38:40.720
Two ways to bill. By snowfall: a price per storm by how much fell. By the hour: men × hours, plus truck, loader, salt and ice melt.

01:38:41.220 --> 01:38:46.153
Labor per man-hour. Each visit bills men × hours at this rate.

01:38:46.653 --> 01:38:50.887
Truck and loader. The plow truck and loader rates per hour.

01:38:51.387 --> 01:38:59.320
Salt, ice melt, walks. Salt per ton and ice melt per bag (by what was used), and a price per visit for walks.

01:38:59.820 --> 01:39:03.187
By snowfall. Switch to snowfall pricing.

01:39:03.687 --> 01:39:13.153
Snowfall bands. A price per storm for each band (0" to 1.99", 2" to 3.99" …). The x removes a band.

01:39:13.653 --> 01:39:16.520
Add a band. Adds the next band.

01:39:17.020 --> 01:39:22.387
Each inch over. Above the last band, this is added for every started inch.

01:39:22.887 --> 01:39:31.020
Salt, calcium, walks. A price each time you salt or put down calcium, and per visit for walks (blank if included).

01:39:31.520 --> 01:39:37.920
Save it. Save pricing keeps it; visits on this plan can then be billed. The tour doesn't press it.

01:39:38.420 --> 01:39:43.087
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:39:43.636 --> 01:39:53.348
Chapter twelve. Timesheets. Each person's week, overtime, missed clock-outs, corrections, approval and the ADP file.

01:39:53.548 --> 01:39:55.781
Everything on Timesheets.

01:39:56.481 --> 01:40:06.781
Timesheets. Each person's week from the crew app: every part of the day, paid hours, overtime after 40 h, missed clock-outs. Breaks are unpaid.

01:40:07.281 --> 01:40:13.681
Pick the week. The arrows go back or forward a week. This week shows up when you are on an older week.

01:40:14.181 --> 01:40:21.515
Add time. Adds a forgotten punch or a paper timesheet. Tour: "Fix a missed clock-out or add time".

01:40:22.015 --> 01:40:29.281
Approve the week. Approves everyone whose week has no missed clock-out. Payroll gets approved hours only.

01:40:29.781 --> 01:40:39.348
Weekly job tracker. The paper landscape job tracker, filled in from the crew app: each day, each job with start, end, men and man-hours.

01:40:39.848 --> 01:40:42.515
Crew. One crew, or all of them.

01:40:43.015 --> 01:40:45.248
Print. Prints the tracker.

01:40:45.781 --> 01:40:50.448
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:40:50.948 --> 01:41:02.515
ADP export. Shows the approved week as pay data for ADP Workforce Now, to copy or download. Set the ADP company code under Settings first.

01:41:02.981 --> 01:41:07.581
Paid hours. Paid hours for everyone this week (breaks left out).

01:41:08.081 --> 01:41:12.648
Overtime. Hours past 40 in the week, across all jobs.

01:41:13.148 --> 01:41:21.281
On jobs. The share of paid time on site. Yard, loading and travel are shared across the day's jobs for costing.

01:41:21.781 --> 01:41:28.715
Missed clock-outs. Missed clock-outs to fix before approving. When there are none, how many people are approved.

01:41:29.215 --> 01:41:38.781
The colours. Yard, Loading, Travel, On a job, Unloading, Break. Click a block in a ribbon to correct it; ✎ = corrected by the office.

01:41:39.248 --> 01:41:51.448
One person's week. Name, ADP file #, paid hours (regular + OT), hours on jobs, shop, travel and breaks. Click the row to fold or open the days.

01:41:51.948 --> 01:41:56.615
Their state. Missed clock-out (fix it first), To approve, or Approved.

01:41:57.115 --> 01:42:04.148
Approve one person. Approves just this person's week. An approved week shows an undo arrow instead.

01:42:04.648 --> 01:42:10.915
ADP file #. The person's file number in ADP; the export uses it.

01:42:11.415 --> 01:42:16.015
File #. Type it as it is in ADP Workforce Now.

01:42:16.515 --> 01:42:20.181
Save it. Save keeps it. The tour doesn't press it.

01:42:20.681 --> 01:42:25.348
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:42:25.848 --> 01:42:36.915
A day as a ribbon. 5 am to 9 pm; each block is a part of the day, and the day's paid total is on the right. Hover a block for its times and job.

01:42:37.381 --> 01:42:43.781
A missed clock-out. The red dashed block never closed. Click it to put in the real end time.

01:42:44.132 --> 01:42:47.032
Fix a missed clock-out or add time.

01:42:47.732 --> 01:42:51.299
A missed clock-out. Click the red dashed block.

01:42:51.799 --> 01:42:56.699
No clock-out. It says when the block started and that it was never closed.

01:42:57.199 --> 01:43:01.932
What. Yard, Loading, Travel, On a job, Unloading or Break.

01:43:02.432 --> 01:43:06.299
Start. When it started, on the company clock (Eastern).

01:43:06.799 --> 01:43:11.665
End. When they really finished. For a block still running, leave it empty.

01:43:12.165 --> 01:43:17.399
Job. For On a job: which job. The hours go to that job's costing.

01:43:17.899 --> 01:43:25.999
Why. Why it changed, e.g. Forgot to clock out; left at 4:30 per the lead. The original times are kept too.

01:43:26.499 --> 01:43:30.932
Remove this entry. Takes the block off their week (it asks first).

01:43:31.432 --> 01:43:38.899
Save the correction. Save correction marks it ✎. If the week was approved, approve it again. The tour doesn't press it.

01:43:39.399 --> 01:43:44.065
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:43:44.565 --> 01:43:48.599
Add time. For a forgotten punch or a paper timesheet.

01:43:49.099 --> 01:43:51.032
Who. The person.

01:43:51.699 --> 01:43:53.699
Day. The day.

01:43:54.299 --> 01:43:59.032
What. Yard, Loading, Travel, On a job, Unloading or Break.

01:43:59.532 --> 01:44:05.199
From and to. The start and end times. Split a shift that runs past midnight.

01:44:05.699 --> 01:44:08.665
Job. For On a job: which job.

01:44:09.165 --> 01:44:13.032
Note. e.g. Paper timesheet · phone was dead.

01:44:13.532 --> 01:44:19.532
Add it. Add time adds it, shown as corrected by the office. The tour doesn't press it.

01:44:20.032 --> 01:44:24.699
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

01:44:25.199 --> 01:44:32.065
Correct any block. Any block opens the same form: change what it was, its times or its job.

01:44:32.615 --> 01:44:41.260
Chapter thirteen. Invoices. Drafts, sending, payments, cards, month-end billing and the QuickBooks file.

01:44:41.460 --> 01:44:43.793
Everything on Invoices.

01:44:44.493 --> 01:44:52.293
Invoices. Every bill in one place. The line under the title is the total still open across all customers.

01:44:52.793 --> 01:45:01.860
QuickBooks export. Makes the files QuickBooks Online imports: customers, invoices or payments for a date range. Let's open it.

01:45:02.327 --> 01:45:15.127
Customers, invoices or payments. Pick what goes in the file. Export customers before invoices so the names match in QuickBooks. Payments come out as a deposit list for the bookkeeper.

01:45:15.627 --> 01:45:25.893
Make the file. Builds the file for the dates you pick, then offers Download and Copy. The QuickBooks tour shows every option. The tour doesn't make a file.

01:45:26.393 --> 01:45:30.727
Close the panel. The X closes it without exporting anything.

01:45:31.227 --> 01:45:40.093
New invoice. For work outside a job: a service call, extras. Job invoices come from the job's payment schedule instead.

01:45:40.593 --> 01:45:51.260
Which customer?. Type a name, phone or street. Clicking a customer in the list makes a new draft invoice for them right away and opens it, ready for its lines.

01:45:51.727 --> 01:45:57.693
Close it. Close it if you only wanted to look. Nothing is made until you pick a customer.

01:45:58.193 --> 01:46:10.727
How late the money is. Open money by age. Current is not due yet; 1-30 and 31-60 days late turn amber; 61-90 and Over 90 turn red.

01:46:11.227 --> 01:46:24.827
Month-end run. When customers billed monthly have finished jobs, a Month-end run bar shows above the tabs. Create … invoices makes the drafts after asking. No bar = nothing to bill.

01:46:25.327 --> 01:46:38.293
Maintenance to bill. Finished maintenance visits and monthly fees show in a green bar. Create the invoices makes one draft per customer, a line per visit or month, with no extra question.

01:46:38.793 --> 01:46:46.760
Drafts. Invoices not sent yet. Open one to change the lines, dates and note, then Email now or Print now.

01:46:47.227 --> 01:46:53.460
Open. Sent and not fully paid, overdue ones included. The list to work from every day.

01:46:53.960 --> 01:46:59.827
Overdue. Past the due date. The red number next to the status is how many days late.

01:47:00.327 --> 01:47:02.460
Paid. Paid in full.

01:47:02.960 --> 01:47:07.193
All. Every invoice: drafts, open, paid and void.

01:47:07.693 --> 01:47:14.393
Search the list. Type an invoice number, customer or job number. It filters the tab you're on.

01:47:14.893 --> 01:47:20.493
Back to Open. Charging cards on file works from the Open and Overdue tabs.

01:47:20.993 --> 01:47:33.660
Charge cards on file. When open invoices have a card on file, rows get a tick box and 'Select all with a card' shows here. Then 'Charge N cards' charges them in one batch, after asking.

01:47:34.127 --> 01:47:47.093
The columns. Invoice number with its kind and job, the customer (💳 = card on file), date issued, status with days late and emailed or printed, the total and what's still open.

01:47:47.593 --> 01:47:57.227
Open an invoice. Click any row to open it: lines, the customer copy, payments. The tour 'Everything on an invoice' walks through that screen.

01:47:57.577 --> 01:47:59.810
Everything on an invoice.

01:48:00.510 --> 01:48:05.777
Open an invoice. Click any invoice in the list. We'll open an overdue one.

01:48:06.277 --> 01:48:11.544
Back to the customer. The customer's name above the number opens their screen.

01:48:12.044 --> 01:48:23.144
Number, status and dates. Next to it: the kind of invoice and its job, the status, the date issued, when it's due (or due on receipt) and when it was emailed or printed.

01:48:23.644 --> 01:48:34.344
Email. Emails the invoice to the customer. On a draft it's Email now and marks it sent. While live email is off it goes to the test address instead.

01:48:34.844 --> 01:48:41.644
Print. Prints it exactly as the customer gets it. On a draft it's Print now and marks it sent (printed).

01:48:42.144 --> 01:48:48.444
Record payment. A check, cash, card or bank transfer came in. Let's open the form.

01:48:48.944 --> 01:48:55.610
Amount. Starts at what's still open. Enter less for a part payment. It can't be more than what's open.

01:48:56.110 --> 01:49:05.777
Method. Check, Card, Cash, Bank transfer or Other. With Card, the card fee from Settings shows as its own surcharge; untick it to waive it.

01:49:06.277 --> 01:49:13.244
Check # / reference. The check number or a reference, so the bookkeeper can match it to the deposit.

01:49:13.744 --> 01:49:18.444
Received. The day the money came in. Today unless you change it.

01:49:18.944 --> 01:49:29.410
Save the payment. Record payment saves it: the invoice shows what's left or Paid in full, and the customer's balance updates. The tour doesn't save it.

01:49:29.910 --> 01:49:35.044
Close the form. The X (or Cancel) closes it without recording anything.

01:49:35.544 --> 01:49:46.610
Card on file. If the customer has a card on file, 'Charge card ••1234' and Card declined show here. Charge card charges what's open, after asking.

01:49:47.077 --> 01:49:59.744
Card declined, void. Card declined logs a decline: the customer is asked to update the card and the office gets a call. Before any payment, a bin icon here voids the invoice.

01:50:00.244 --> 01:50:09.644
Test mode. Shows while live email is off: emails go to the test address, not the customer. Turn live email on in Settings, Email.

01:50:10.144 --> 01:50:20.044
Lines. What's billed: description, quantity, price, taxable or not, amount. A sent invoice is locked; to change it, void it and make a new one.

01:50:20.544 --> 01:50:29.910
The customer copy. Exactly what the customer gets by email or on paper. The invoice total and their account balance are kept apart.

01:50:30.410 --> 01:50:35.310
Open full size. Opens the customer copy full width to read it.

01:50:35.810 --> 01:50:45.777
Print / PDF. Prints this copy; choose Save as PDF in the print window to attach it to your own email. This doesn't mark the invoice sent.

01:50:46.277 --> 01:50:49.844
Close it. The X closes the full-size copy.

01:50:50.344 --> 01:50:55.610
Print / PDF. The same print or PDF, straight from the card.

01:50:56.110 --> 01:51:03.977
This invoice. Subtotal, sales tax, the invoice total, what's been paid, and what's still due on this invoice alone.

01:51:04.477 --> 01:51:13.644
The customer's account. When they have other open invoices, an account box shows the whole balance and lists the others (click one to open it).

01:51:14.110 --> 01:51:22.244
Payments. Every payment on this invoice: date, method, check number or batch, who recorded it, and any card surcharge.

01:51:22.744 --> 01:51:32.110
Reminders. Past-due reminders and other messages about this invoice: sent, waiting or skipped, and when. They're set up on Automations.

01:51:32.460 --> 01:51:35.827
Invoice, record a payment, chase what's owed.

01:51:36.527 --> 01:51:43.727
Open an invoice. Invoices come from the job: a payment-schedule step, the balance, or a change order.

01:51:44.227 --> 01:51:53.660
Record a payment. Check, cash, ACH or card. A card payment adds the card fee as its own line; the job's balance updates.

01:51:54.160 --> 01:52:03.760
Who owes what. Open invoices by customer and by age: 0–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+.

01:52:04.260 --> 01:52:08.527
The call list. Print it every couple of weeks for the office to call.

01:52:08.877 --> 01:52:12.310
Check a draft invoice, then email or print it.

01:52:13.010 --> 01:52:20.010
Drafts. Invoices not sent yet: from a job's payment schedule, the month-end run or New invoice.

01:52:20.510 --> 01:52:23.844
Open a draft. Click the draft to open it.

01:52:24.344 --> 01:52:32.544
Lines. A draft can be changed until it's sent. Each line: description, quantity, price, a Tax tick and the amount.

01:52:33.044 --> 01:52:43.444
Change a line. Type straight into the boxes; the amount updates as you type. Untick Tax for a tax-exempt line. The X at the end removes the line.

01:52:43.944 --> 01:52:47.510
Add line. Adds an empty line at the bottom.

01:52:48.010 --> 01:52:51.544
Invoice date. The date printed on the invoice.

01:52:52.044 --> 01:53:00.377
Due. The same day as the invoice date reads 'due on receipt'. A later date prints as the due date and counts for overdue.

01:53:00.877 --> 01:53:07.144
Note on the invoice. Printed on the invoice: a thank-you, who to make checks payable to.

01:53:07.644 --> 01:53:15.477
Save draft. Saves your changes. Every line needs a description, and the due date can't be before the invoice date.

01:53:15.977 --> 01:53:25.244
Email now. Saves any changes, emails it to the customer and marks it sent. While live email is off it goes to the test address.

01:53:25.744 --> 01:53:30.577
Print now. Saves, opens the print window and marks it sent (printed).

01:53:31.077 --> 01:53:36.477
Preview. The customer copy. After changing lines, save to refresh it.

01:53:36.977 --> 01:53:46.710
The customer's account. Their whole balance across every open invoice, kept apart from this invoice. Click another invoice listed here to open it.

01:53:47.210 --> 01:53:57.944
Void. Voids it, after asking. It stays on file as void, and a job milestone it billed can be invoiced again. Only before any payment is recorded.

01:53:58.293 --> 01:54:02.093
Email or print all the draft invoices at once.

01:54:02.793 --> 01:54:08.193
Drafts. The invoices not sent yet, for example after the month-end run.

01:54:08.693 --> 01:54:18.793
Email all. Emails each customer their own invoice, one after another. Any customer without an email address is listed so you can print theirs.

01:54:19.293 --> 01:54:24.360
Print all. One print job with every draft, a page each; they're marked sent.

01:54:24.710 --> 01:54:28.477
Month-end billing: monthly accounts and maintenance.

01:54:29.177 --> 01:54:40.810
Month-end run. Customers set to 'Invoicing: Monthly' get their completed jobs billed at month end. This bar lists them with the total. No bar = nothing to bill.

01:54:41.310 --> 01:54:52.177
Create the drafts. Create … invoices asks first, then makes one draft per job. They land on the Drafts tab to check before sending. The tour doesn't press it.

01:54:52.677 --> 01:55:01.443
Maintenance to bill. Finished maintenance visits and monthly fees waiting to be billed, with how many customers and the amount before tax.

01:55:01.943 --> 01:55:12.210
Create the invoices. Makes one draft per customer straight away, a line per visit or monthly fee. They land on Drafts too. The tour doesn't press it.

01:55:12.710 --> 01:55:17.477
Check the drafts. Every new month-end invoice waits here as a draft.

01:55:17.977 --> 01:55:26.777
Open, check, send. Open each draft, check the lines, then Email now or Print now. That marks it sent and it moves to Open.

01:55:27.127 --> 01:55:31.794
Charge cards on file, one or many, and log a declined card.

01:55:32.494 --> 01:55:37.694
Open invoices. Cards are charged from the Open or Overdue tab.

01:55:38.194 --> 01:55:48.494
Who has a card on file. A 💳 and the last 4 digits next to the customer means a card is on file. Those rows get a tick box on the left.

01:55:48.994 --> 01:56:01.060
Charge many at once. 'Select all with a card' ticks them all (or tick rows one by one). 'Charge N cards' charges what's open on each and records card payments, after asking.

01:56:01.527 --> 01:56:05.994
Or one invoice. Open the invoice to charge just that one.

01:56:06.494 --> 01:56:17.960
Charge card. With a card on file and money open, 'Charge card ••1234' shows here. It charges what's still open and records it as a card payment, after asking.

01:56:18.460 --> 01:56:31.127
Card declined. Declined at the terminal or in the batch? Card declined: note what the processor said. Record it emails the customer to update the card and puts a call on the office list.

01:56:31.594 --> 01:56:36.127
Paid by card at the terminal. Record payment, then pick Card.

01:56:36.627 --> 01:56:47.527
Card and the surcharge. With Card picked, the card fee from Settings (Contract terms) shows as its own surcharge before you record it. Untick it to waive the fee.

01:56:48.027 --> 01:56:52.194
Close. The X closes the form without recording anything.

01:56:52.543 --> 01:56:55.110
Make the QuickBooks export file.

01:56:55.810 --> 01:57:03.543
QuickBooks export. Until QuickBooks is connected directly, the office sends it files. Open the export panel.

01:57:04.043 --> 01:57:11.943
Where it goes. In QuickBooks Online: Settings, then Import data. This line also says when you last exported.

01:57:12.443 --> 01:57:19.810
Customers first. Export customers before invoices, so every invoice finds its customer in QuickBooks.

01:57:20.310 --> 01:57:26.676
Then invoices. The invoices sent in the date range, ready for QuickBooks' invoice import.

01:57:27.176 --> 01:57:35.643
Payments. Payments received in the range, as a deposit list the bookkeeper matches to the bank. Click it when that's the file you need.

01:57:36.143 --> 01:57:43.176
From and To. The date range. It starts on the 1st of this month and runs to today; change either date.

01:57:43.676 --> 01:57:52.043
Only what wasn't exported yet. Leave it ticked so nothing goes into QuickBooks twice. Untick it to export the whole range again.

01:57:52.543 --> 01:58:00.276
Mark these as exported. Remembers what went into this file, so 'Only what wasn't exported yet' skips it next time.

01:58:00.776 --> 01:58:12.243
Make the file. Builds the file and shows its name and row count, with Download (a .csv file) and Copy. Then import it in QuickBooks. The tour doesn't make one.

01:58:12.743 --> 01:58:15.510
Close. The X closes the panel.

01:58:16.060 --> 01:58:24.599
Chapter fourteen. Reports. Sales, commissions and job costing by job, salesperson and crew.

01:58:24.799 --> 01:58:26.999
Everything on Reports.

01:58:27.699 --> 01:58:37.066
Reports. The year's numbers: sales, salespeople, money owed, commissions and job profit. Only roles that see money can open it.

01:58:37.566 --> 01:58:44.166
Sales to date. Invoiced this year before tax, and how it compares with the same point last year.

01:58:44.666 --> 01:58:49.899
Won this year. Estimates won this year, before tax, and how many jobs.

01:58:50.399 --> 01:58:54.666
Close rate. Won out of won plus lost estimates this year.

01:58:55.166 --> 01:59:02.166
Owed to us. Everything open on invoices and how much is past due. Click it to jump to Money owed.

01:59:02.666 --> 01:59:12.232
Sales by month. The Sales tab: this year's bars next to last year's, month by month, invoiced before tax. Hover a bar for the amount.

01:59:12.732 --> 01:59:18.566
Export. Every table here has Export: it downloads the numbers as an Excel file.

01:59:19.066 --> 01:59:26.732
Won by category. What sells: estimate sections won this year, by catalogue category (or the section name).

01:59:27.232 --> 01:59:30.299
Salespeople. Each salesperson's year.

01:59:30.799 --> 01:59:41.299
Each salesperson. Won and lost by decision date, jobs, close rate, and what's out now (open estimates: amount and how many). Export it for Excel.

01:59:41.799 --> 01:59:45.099
Money owed. Who owes what, and how late.

01:59:45.599 --> 01:59:54.999
By age. All customers together: Current, then 1-30, 31-60, 61-90 and Over 90 days past due.

01:59:55.499 --> 02:00:05.632
Print the call list. Every week or two: each customer who owes, oldest past due first, with phone numbers and room to note the call. The tour doesn't print.

02:00:06.132 --> 02:00:14.632
By customer. One row per customer, split by age, with the total. Click a customer to open them. Export it for Excel.

02:00:15.132 --> 02:00:18.132
Commissions. What salespeople have earned.

02:00:18.632 --> 02:00:28.566
Earned and paid. Per salesperson: earned but not paid yet, and paid this year. The line above says how it's worked out; rates are in Settings, Money.

02:00:29.066 --> 02:00:36.432
Mark paid. After you pay a salesperson, Mark paid moves all their earned entries to paid. It asks first.

02:00:36.932 --> 02:00:47.932
Commission report. One row per job with the commission on it, filtered by salesperson and dates, and exported for payroll. The commissions tour covers each filter.

02:00:48.432 --> 02:00:51.566
Job costing. Profit on each job.

02:00:52.066 --> 02:00:59.832
Date range. This month, last month, this year, last year or the last 12 months. The dates in use show next to it.

02:01:00.332 --> 02:01:12.699
Revenue, costs, profit, hours. Revenue with change orders, job costs (labor at the burn rate, materials, subs), gross profit and margin, and crew hours against the estimate.

02:01:13.199 --> 02:01:24.266
Job profit. Each job finished in the range, plus those still running: revenue, cost, hours, profit, margin against the estimate. Click a job to open it.

02:01:24.732 --> 02:01:35.399
Jobs, salespeople or crews. Adds the same numbers up by salesperson or by crew instead of by job. Export downloads every job's details.

02:01:35.866 --> 02:01:47.666
Burn rates. What one man-hour costs: wages, taxes, comp, benefits, overhead. Owner and office add a New rate from a date. The job costing tour shows the form.

02:01:48.166 --> 02:01:51.566
Timesheets. Crew hours have their own screen.

02:01:52.066 --> 02:02:03.199
Open Timesheets. Each person's week from the crew app: every segment, overtime past 40 h, missed clock-outs, corrections, approval and the ADP export.

02:02:03.549 --> 02:02:07.782
Commission report: filter, check, export for payroll.

02:02:08.482 --> 02:02:12.282
Commissions. Open the Commissions tab on Reports.

02:02:12.782 --> 02:02:23.749
Earned and paid. The salesperson on the estimate earns it. The line above says when and on what (profit or sale); rates per salesperson are in Settings, Money.

02:02:24.249 --> 02:02:32.982
Mark paid. After paying a salesperson, Mark paid moves all their earned entries to paid, after asking. The tour doesn't press it.

02:02:33.482 --> 02:02:42.649
Commission report. Every job by salesperson: contract, change orders, invoiced, paid, paid in full, and the commission on it.

02:02:43.116 --> 02:02:51.482
Salesperson. Every salesperson, or pick one. Owner and office see this filter; a salesperson sees their own jobs.

02:02:51.982 --> 02:02:59.582
Which date. Paid in full between, Completed between or Sold between: the date the range below filters on.

02:03:00.082 --> 02:03:08.549
From and To. The date range. It starts at January 1st of this year through today. The list updates as soon as you change it.

02:03:09.049 --> 02:03:17.116
Only jobs paid in full. Untick it to see every job in the range, paid or not; unpaid ones show 'Not yet'.

02:03:17.582 --> 02:03:30.782
One row per job. Contract, change orders, completed, invoiced, paid, paid-in-full date, the base (profit or sale), rate and commission, with its status. Click the customer to open the job.

02:03:31.282 --> 02:03:39.616
Totals. The totals for everything in the list: jobs, contract, change orders, invoiced, paid, profit and commission.

02:03:40.116 --> 02:03:47.916
Export for payroll. Downloads the report as an Excel file, one row per job. The tour doesn't download it.

02:03:48.266 --> 02:03:50.366
Commissions report.

02:03:51.066 --> 02:03:58.866
Commissions. Completed, paid-in-full jobs per salesperson ("sold by" on the estimate), with the rate and the amount.

02:03:59.366 --> 02:04:02.366
For Excel. Export it for payroll.

02:04:02.716 --> 02:04:06.983
Job costing: profit by job, salesperson and crew.

02:04:07.683 --> 02:04:12.216
Job costing. Open the Job costing tab on Reports.

02:04:12.716 --> 02:04:20.583
Pick the dates. This month, last month, this year, last year or the last 12 months. The dates in use show next to it.

02:04:21.083 --> 02:04:26.249
Last 12 months. Click a range and the whole tab recalculates for it.

02:04:26.749 --> 02:04:38.116
Revenue. Contracts plus approved change orders for jobs with costs. Jobs with no crew time or costs yet aren't counted, so they don't show a false 100%.

02:04:38.616 --> 02:04:44.449
Job costs. Crew hours at the burn rate, plus materials and subcontractors.

02:04:44.949 --> 02:04:49.449
Gross profit. Revenue minus job costs, and the margin.

02:04:49.949 --> 02:04:57.116
Crew hours. Hours the crews logged against the hours estimated. Going over is what eats the margin.

02:04:57.616 --> 02:05:02.283
Job profit. Jobs finished in the range plus those still running.

02:05:02.783 --> 02:05:14.716
One job. CO = change orders in the revenue. Red hours = more than estimated. Margin shows the estimate's margin next to it. Click a job to open it.

02:05:15.216 --> 02:05:19.783
By salesperson. The same numbers added up per salesperson.

02:05:20.283 --> 02:05:25.049
By crew. Per crew. A job two crews worked on counts for both.

02:05:25.549 --> 02:05:28.949
Back to jobs. One row per job again.

02:05:29.449 --> 02:05:40.016
Export. Downloads every job as an Excel file: estimated and actual hours, labor, material, subs, other, total cost, profit and margins.

02:05:40.483 --> 02:05:51.816
Burn rates. What one man-hour costs: wages, payroll taxes, workers' comp, benefits and overhead. Types of work without their own rate use the company-wide one.

02:05:52.316 --> 02:06:00.883
Rate cards. Each card: the rate today and since when. A rate that starts later shows in amber; History lists older rates.

02:06:01.383 --> 02:06:07.416
New rate. Owner and office can add a rate, for example when wages or comp change.

02:06:07.916 --> 02:06:13.116
For. Company-wide, or one type of work such as Hardscape or Landscape.

02:06:13.616 --> 02:06:17.483
Per man-hour. The full cost of one man-hour, all in.

02:06:17.983 --> 02:06:23.449
From. Work from this date costs at the new rate. Earlier work keeps the rate it had.

02:06:23.949 --> 02:06:29.249
Note. What's in it, for example '2027 wages + comp'.

02:06:29.749 --> 02:06:35.716
Save rate. Saves the rate and job profit recalculates. The tour doesn't save it.

02:06:36.216 --> 02:06:39.583
Close. The X closes the form without saving.

02:06:40.132 --> 02:06:47.519
Chapter fifteen. Catalogue. Services, materials and the kits that price an estimate.

02:06:47.719 --> 02:06:49.986
Everything on Catalogue.

02:06:50.686 --> 02:07:02.152
Catalogue. Every service, material, equipment item and fee your estimates pick from (Service Autopilot's products). The number under the title counts the active items.

02:07:02.652 --> 02:07:09.752
Add an item. New item opens a blank form. Only people who see money can add or change items.

02:07:10.252 --> 02:07:15.719
Name. The name on estimates and in the list. It's the only thing you must fill in.

02:07:16.219 --> 02:07:26.519
Kind. Service (labor), Material, Equipment or Fee. Only a service can carry a kit of materials. The Kind filter on the list uses it too.

02:07:27.019 --> 02:07:36.686
Category. Hardscape, Plants, Irrigation… It groups the list. A crew whose kind of work matches the category gets won sections of it first.

02:07:37.186 --> 02:07:43.919
Unit. What one of it is: ea, sq ft, ton, job. The quantity on an estimate counts these.

02:07:44.419 --> 02:07:54.252
Cost and price. Price is what the customer pays per unit; Cost, just before it, is what it costs you. The list works out the margin from the two.

02:07:54.752 --> 02:08:04.619
Crew-hours per unit. How many crew-hours one unit takes. It fills the hours on estimates, and the schedule turns those hours into days for a crew.

02:08:05.119 --> 02:08:12.319
Description. What the customer reads on the estimate line. It fills in when the item is added to an estimate.

02:08:12.819 --> 02:08:18.986
Taxable. Ticked: sales tax applies to it. Untick it for items that are never taxed.

02:08:19.486 --> 02:08:29.752
Active. Active items are offered in estimates. Untick to retire one: estimates that have it keep it, and the list hides it unless Show inactive is ticked.

02:08:30.252 --> 02:08:39.019
Add item. Add item saves it (prices can't be negative). Cancel, or the X at the top, closes the form without saving.

02:08:39.519 --> 02:08:43.686
Close the form. The tour closes it without saving anything.

02:08:44.186 --> 02:08:52.252
Search the catalogue. Type part of a name, an item code or a word from the description; the list narrows as you type.

02:08:52.719 --> 02:08:58.086
Filter by kind. Show only services, materials, equipment or fees.

02:08:58.586 --> 02:09:05.719
Filter by category. Show one category. The number beside each category is how many items it has.

02:09:06.219 --> 02:09:12.086
Show inactive. Tick it to include the items you switched off. They carry an Inactive tag.

02:09:12.586 --> 02:09:24.619
The list. Each row: name, code and description, category, kind, unit, and Used (how many estimate lines use it). Click a row to change the item. 60 rows a page.

02:09:25.119 --> 02:09:35.186
Cost, price and margin. Cost, Price and Margin show only for people who see money. A margin in red means the price is below the cost.

02:09:35.652 --> 02:09:45.452
Open an item. Click a row to open the same form, filled in. Changing a price never changes estimates already written. Here: a service.

02:09:45.952 --> 02:09:57.819
A service's kit. Its kit: the materials that come with this service on every estimate, hidden from the customer unless ticked. The tour "Set up a service's kit" shows each part.

02:09:58.319 --> 02:10:03.019
Close it. The tour closes it without saving. That's the whole Catalogue.

02:10:03.369 --> 02:10:06.169
Set up a service's kit of materials.

02:10:06.869 --> 02:10:13.436
Find the service. Only services have a kit. Any kind → Services lists just the services.

02:10:13.936 --> 02:10:20.002
Open the service. Click the service to open it. Here: Paver Patio Installation.

02:10:20.502 --> 02:10:27.402
It must be a service. Kind must be Service (labor). A new service gets its kit after its first save.

02:10:27.902 --> 02:10:33.569
The kit. The materials that come with this service on every estimate it is added to.

02:10:34.069 --> 02:10:46.536
How much per unit. How much of the material goes with one unit of the service, e.g. tons of base per sq ft of patio. The estimate works out the amount from the service's quantity.

02:10:47.036 --> 02:10:55.302
Show it to the customer?. Tick Show to list that material on the customer's copy. Unticked, it stays hidden from the customer.

02:10:55.802 --> 02:11:02.236
Take one out. The x takes that material out of the kit. Nothing changes until you press Save.

02:11:02.736 --> 02:11:10.336
Add a material. Pick a material, equipment item or fee to add it to the kit at 1 per unit, then set the amount.

02:11:10.836 --> 02:11:18.269
Save. Save keeps the item and its kit. New estimates get the new kit; estimates already written don't change.

02:11:18.769 --> 02:11:21.969
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

02:11:22.519 --> 02:11:30.460
Chapter sixteen. Fleet. Trucks and machines: what is due, the service log and the crews' reports.

02:11:30.660 --> 02:11:32.727
Everything on Fleet.

02:11:33.427 --> 02:11:45.460
Fleet & equipment. Every truck and machine: how many, how many are overdue or due soon, and the fleet manager, who gets the Monday due list and the crews' truck reports (set in Settings).

02:11:45.960 --> 02:11:57.127
Log service. Records an oil change, inspection, tire service or repair for any unit. The tour "Log a service, oil change or repair" shows the form.

02:11:57.593 --> 02:12:05.993
Add unit. Adds a truck or machine with its service intervals. The tour "Add or change a truck or machine" shows the form.

02:12:06.493 --> 02:12:16.460
Reported by the crews. Problems crew leads report from the phone (the truck form under More), with photos. The fleet manager hears about them right away.

02:12:16.960 --> 02:12:24.827
Log the fix. Opens Log service for that unit with the problem filled in. Logging the fix closes the report.

02:12:25.327 --> 02:12:31.627
Close without a fix. The x closes a report that needs no repair. Nothing is logged.

02:12:32.127 --> 02:12:42.093
Filter the units. All (everything not sold), Overdue, Due soon, Trucks, Equipment and Sold. The numbers say how many are overdue and due soon.

02:12:42.593 --> 02:12:46.093
Overdue. Only the units with something past due.

02:12:46.593 --> 02:12:50.660
All. Back to every unit. Sold ones stay under Sold.

02:12:51.160 --> 02:13:04.427
A truck. Oil and Tires: miles left (red = over). Inspect: the next inspection. Miles: the last odometer. A red card has something overdue, an amber one something due soon.

02:13:04.927 --> 02:13:15.293
A machine. Machines count engine hours. Service: hours left to the next service. Hours: the meter. L and R track: the hours on each track.

02:13:15.793 --> 02:13:19.093
Open a unit. Click a unit to open it.

02:13:19.593 --> 02:13:28.460
Its details. Vehicle, type, VIN or serial, plate, crew or driver, status, what its maintenance has cost and notes.

02:13:28.960 --> 02:13:38.027
New reading. Type today's odometer (engine hours for a machine) so the due dates stay right. The date of the last reading is below.

02:13:38.493 --> 02:13:45.327
Fix a wrong reading. Tick it only to correct a typo: it allows a number lower than the last reading.

02:13:45.827 --> 02:13:50.293
Save reading. Saves the number and works out again what is due.

02:13:50.793 --> 02:13:58.560
Service history. Every service on this unit: date, service, miles or hours, the work, who did it and the cost.

02:13:59.060 --> 02:14:03.860
Edit unit. Changes its details and intervals, or marks it Sold.

02:14:04.360 --> 02:14:11.093
Log service for this unit. Opens the service form with this unit and its last reading filled in.

02:14:11.593 --> 02:14:14.160
Close it. The tour closes it.

02:14:14.660 --> 02:14:25.427
Service log. Everything serviced in the last 13 months, newest first: date, unit, service, work, miles or hours and cost. 20 rows a page.

02:14:25.777 --> 02:14:28.410
Add or change a truck or machine.

02:14:29.110 --> 02:14:34.044
Add unit. Opens the form. Its fields match your fleet spreadsheet.

02:14:34.544 --> 02:14:42.744
Unit number. The number on the truck or machine (T-01, E-02). It's the only thing you must fill in.

02:14:43.244 --> 02:14:51.310
Truck or equipment. Truck / vehicle counts miles (oil, tires, inspection). Equipment counts engine hours.

02:14:51.810 --> 02:14:56.944
Type. Dump truck, pickup, skid steer… It shows under the name on its card.

02:14:57.444 --> 02:15:05.877
Status. Active, In shop, Out of service, Spare, Reserved or Sold. Sold units leave the main list (see them under Sold).

02:15:06.377 --> 02:15:12.144
Year, make, model, VIN. Year, make and model, then the VIN or serial number.

02:15:12.644 --> 02:15:14.977
Plate. The licence plate.

02:15:15.477 --> 02:15:21.777
Crew or driver. The crew that usually takes it, or a driver's name. Its card shows it.

02:15:22.277 --> 02:15:29.110
Next inspection. The date of the next inspection. It shows amber when close and red when past.

02:15:29.610 --> 02:15:37.577
Oil every. Miles between oil changes. The next one is due this many miles after the last oil change you log.

02:15:38.044 --> 02:15:41.877
Tires every. Miles between tire services.

02:15:42.377 --> 02:15:47.610
Equipment service every. Engine hours between services, for machines.

02:15:48.110 --> 02:15:51.210
Notes. Anything else worth knowing about it.

02:15:51.710 --> 02:15:57.344
Add unit. Saves it. Then log its last oil change so its due dates start.

02:15:57.844 --> 02:16:01.577
Close the form. The tour closes it without saving.

02:16:02.077 --> 02:16:05.344
Change a unit. To change one, open it…

02:16:05.844 --> 02:16:10.377
Edit unit. …and press Edit unit: the same form, filled in.

02:16:10.877 --> 02:16:18.444
Remove unit. Owner or office only. It asks first. Mark the unit Sold instead to keep its history.

02:16:18.944 --> 02:16:21.710
Save. Save keeps the changes.

02:16:22.210 --> 02:16:25.410
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

02:16:25.760 --> 02:16:29.093
Log a service, oil change or repair.

02:16:29.793 --> 02:16:32.960
Log service. Opens the service form.

02:16:33.460 --> 02:16:36.093
Unit. Pick the truck or machine.

02:16:36.593 --> 02:16:39.960
Date. When it was done. It starts at today.

02:16:40.427 --> 02:16:53.193
Service. Oil & Filter, Tire Rotation, Brakes, Annual Inspection, Repair, Seasonal, Track Replacement or Other. Oil, inspection and tire services reset that item's due date.

02:16:53.693 --> 02:16:59.960
Which track. For a track replacement: Left, Right or Both. It must be filled in for that service.

02:17:00.460 --> 02:17:10.393
Miles or hours. The odometer for a truck, or the engine hours for a machine, at the service. Opened from a unit, they start at its last reading.

02:17:10.893 --> 02:17:19.260
Parts and labor. What the parts and the labor cost. Together they make the cost in the service log and the unit's maintenance cost.

02:17:19.760 --> 02:17:23.293
Work performed. What was done, in a few words.

02:17:23.793 --> 02:17:26.960
Performed by. The shop or the mechanic.

02:17:27.460 --> 02:17:30.993
Next due. Optional: a date for the next one.

02:17:31.493 --> 02:17:35.393
Log service. Saves it and moves the due dates on.

02:17:35.893 --> 02:17:39.627
Close the form. The tour closes it without saving.

02:17:40.127 --> 02:17:46.427
A problem a crew reported. For a problem a crew reported from the phone, use its own button.

02:17:46.927 --> 02:17:50.960
Log the fix. Opens the same form for that unit…

02:17:51.460 --> 02:17:58.293
The problem is filled in. …with "Fixed:" and the problem already written. Logging it closes the report.

02:17:58.793 --> 02:18:01.993
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

02:18:02.544 --> 02:18:10.187
Chapter seventeen. Team and crews. Logins, roles, crews, their leads and their colours.

02:18:10.387 --> 02:18:12.887
Everything on Team & crews.

02:18:13.587 --> 02:18:24.687
Team & crews. Who works here and the crews the schedule plans with. Only the owner and the office open it. The line under the title counts crews and active people.

02:18:25.187 --> 02:18:34.287
New crew. Adds a crew: name, kind of work, lead, size, hours a day, colour and members. The tour "Set up a crew" shows each part.

02:18:34.787 --> 02:18:39.554
Add person. Gives someone a role in the office app or the crew phone app.

02:18:40.054 --> 02:18:44.854
Name. Their name as it shows on appointments, crews and the schedule.

02:18:45.354 --> 02:18:54.320
Login id. Their FieldProxy login (lower case, no spaces). It ties the person to their login and can't be changed later.

02:18:54.820 --> 02:19:06.187
Role. Owner, Office, Sales, Project manager, Crew lead or Field: it decides what they can open. For a new person, the four office roles tick Takes appointments.

02:19:06.687 --> 02:19:08.954
Phone. Their phone number.

02:19:09.454 --> 02:19:17.187
Hourly cost. What an hour of their time costs you; job costing uses it. Only people who see money see this.

02:19:17.687 --> 02:19:26.587
Sees prices and money. Ticked: they see prices, margins, invoices and payments. Unticked: all of that is hidden from them.

02:19:27.087 --> 02:19:34.487
Takes appointments. Ticked: they're in the "With" list when you book a visit or a phone call. A task can go to anyone.

02:19:34.987 --> 02:19:43.620
Office app or phone app. Crew leads and field staff use the crew phone app and never see money there. Office roles open this app.

02:19:44.120 --> 02:19:50.120
Add person. Saves them. Cancel, or the X at the top, closes without saving.

02:19:50.620 --> 02:19:54.354
Close the form. The tour closes it without saving.

02:19:54.854 --> 02:19:57.754
Crews. Your crews, one card each.

02:19:58.254 --> 02:20:10.354
A crew. Its colour on the schedule, kind of work, lead, people × hours a day = the crew-hours a day the schedule checks against, and members (★ = lead). Click it to change it.

02:20:10.854 --> 02:20:21.987
People. Everyone with a role: login ("no login yet" until they have one), role, sees money, takes appointments, the crew they lead and phone. Inactive people are tagged.

02:20:22.487 --> 02:20:30.054
Hourly cost. What each person's hour costs, for job costing. Only people who see money see this column.

02:20:30.554 --> 02:20:35.854
Change a person. Click a person to change their role, access or phone.

02:20:36.354 --> 02:20:41.520
Login id stays. Once saved, the login id can't be changed.

02:20:42.020 --> 02:20:48.087
Active. Untick Active when someone leaves: they come off the pick lists and their history stays.

02:20:48.587 --> 02:20:51.354
Save. Save keeps the changes.

02:20:51.854 --> 02:20:55.054
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

02:20:55.554 --> 02:21:05.820
Logins without a role. FieldProxy logins that have no role here yet. Add each one with Add person, using the same login id, to let them in.

02:21:06.170 --> 02:21:10.337
Set up a crew: lead, size, hours, colour, members.

02:21:11.037 --> 02:21:13.803
New crew. Opens the crew form.

02:21:14.303 --> 02:21:20.237
Crew name. What the schedule calls it, e.g. Hardscape 1. It must be filled in.

02:21:20.737 --> 02:21:32.570
Kind of work. hardscape, landscape, lighting… Won estimate sections from a matching catalogue category get this crew first. Customer notices in Settings go by it too.

02:21:33.070 --> 02:21:37.837
Crew lead. Who leads it (★). The lead is added to the members when you save.

02:21:38.337 --> 02:21:41.770
People on the crew. How many usually work on it.

02:21:42.270 --> 02:21:52.437
Hours a day. Their working day. People × hours = the crew-hours a day; the schedule warns above it. The line under the colours works it out.

02:21:52.903 --> 02:22:02.803
Colour on the schedule. Each crew gets its own colour. A swatch with a dot is taken by another crew: pick one without a dot so crews look different.

02:22:03.303 --> 02:22:09.370
Any other colour. Or pick any colour here. If it looks like another crew's, a red line says so.

02:22:09.870 --> 02:22:12.570
Members. Tick everyone on the crew.

02:22:13.070 --> 02:22:18.303
Add crew. Saves the crew. People and hours a day must be above zero.

02:22:18.803 --> 02:22:22.537
Close the form. The tour closes it without saving.

02:22:23.037 --> 02:22:26.537
Change a crew. To change a crew, click its card.

02:22:27.037 --> 02:22:31.537
Active. Untick to take the crew off the schedule without deleting it.

02:22:32.037 --> 02:22:35.703
Save crew. Saves the changes and the member list.

02:22:36.203 --> 02:22:39.403
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

02:22:39.953 --> 02:22:50.540
Chapter eighteen. Automations. Every message the system sends by itself: on or off, timing, wording, the queue, and setting up sending.

02:22:50.740 --> 02:22:53.173
Everything on Automations.

02:22:53.873 --> 02:23:04.840
Automations. What the system does without anyone pressing a button: follow-ups, reminders and notices. Every message waits in the queue first, where you can stop it.

02:23:05.340 --> 02:23:14.907
At a glance. How many of the 9 automations are switched on, messages sent today and in the last 30 days, and how many are waiting to go.

02:23:15.373 --> 02:23:25.473
Run now. Runs the checks straight away instead of waiting for the next run: whatever is due gets queued and its call tickets made. A message says what it did.

02:23:25.973 --> 02:23:30.840
Wording. Opens the Wording tab: the words of every email and text.

02:23:31.340 --> 02:23:38.040
Today's clock. Each dot is a message sent today, at the hour it went. The red hand is now.

02:23:38.540 --> 02:23:47.140
Engine. Green when the automatic run is connected (every 10 minutes). Until then the checks run whenever the office opens the app.

02:23:47.640 --> 02:23:52.640
Last run. When the checks last ran. Amber if it was over an hour ago.

02:23:53.140 --> 02:23:59.207
Sending. When the last message went out. Amber if a message has waited more than 20 minutes.

02:23:59.707 --> 02:24:07.640
Live email. On: messages go to customers. Off: they go to the test address. Change it under Sending setup.

02:24:08.140 --> 02:24:12.273
Texts. Whether text messages are switched on (Sending setup).

02:24:12.773 --> 02:24:20.240
Online estimates. Whether the online estimate links, where customers view and accept online, are installed.

02:24:20.740 --> 02:24:24.707
What runs. Every automation, with its switch and timing.

02:24:25.207 --> 02:24:37.073
One automation. What it does, its flow (what starts it, the wait, what goes out), its timing, how many went out in 30 days and Edit wording. Change a number and a Save button appears.

02:24:37.573 --> 02:24:47.007
On or off. The switch turns it on or off and saves straight away. The tour "Switch reminders and notices on or off" goes through all nine.

02:24:47.507 --> 02:24:50.240
Queue. Messages waiting to go.

02:24:50.740 --> 02:25:04.273
Waiting to go. Each message, customer, subject and address, and when it goes. The eye shows it, the arrow sends it now, the x cancels it. If its reason goes away (paid, answered) it cancels itself.

02:25:04.773 --> 02:25:06.740
Sent. What went out.

02:25:07.373 --> 02:25:19.207
What went out. The last 80 messages, newest first, with All / Sent / Not sent. The eye shows a message; the round arrow sends a failed, cancelled or skipped one again.

02:25:19.707 --> 02:25:22.673
Wording. The words of every message.

02:25:23.173 --> 02:25:35.607
The words. Pick a message under Every message, change its subject and text, and see it on the right as a customer gets it. The tour "Change the wording of an email or text" shows each part.

02:25:36.107 --> 02:25:40.740
Sending setup. The Sending setup tab: how messages are sent.

02:25:41.240 --> 02:25:53.473
How sending is set up. Live email, the test address, the address customers write to, texts, links in messages, crew photo rules and QuickBooks items. Save setup keeps them.

02:25:53.973 --> 02:25:57.640
Runs. The Runs tab: every run of the checks.

02:25:58.140 --> 02:26:08.940
Automation runs. When each run happened, what started it (the timer, the office or Run now), how long it took and what it did. A red tag means a part failed.

02:26:09.440 --> 02:26:19.440
Online estimate events. Online estimates opened, accepted and declined, as the platform reported them. Click one to open the estimate.

02:26:19.790 --> 02:26:24.257
Switch reminders and notices on or off, and set their timing.

02:26:24.957 --> 02:26:28.523
What runs. Every automation, one card each.

02:26:29.023 --> 02:26:41.223
Estimate follow-ups. No answer to an estimate: Email 1 after the days you set, Email 2 later, then a call ticket for the office. Estimates older than the last number are skipped.

02:26:41.723 --> 02:26:45.290
The switch. Turns it on or off and saves at once.

02:26:45.790 --> 02:26:53.323
Its timing. Change a number and the flow above follows it. Press the Save button that appears on the card to keep it.

02:26:53.823 --> 02:27:08.123
Past-due reminders. One statement per customer listing what's open: first after the days past due, then every few days, up to the number set; then a collection call. It can include SA balances.

02:27:08.623 --> 02:27:21.390
Appointment reminders. The day before, at the hour you set (0–23, 10 = 10 am), by email and by text when texts are on. Moving the appointment sends the new time.

02:27:21.890 --> 02:27:32.090
Job start notice. The day before a crew's first day on a job. "Crews usually arrive" is the wording for when they come. Maintenance visits don't get one.

02:27:32.590 --> 02:27:40.057
"We've arrived". Sent when the crew lead starts the job on the phone, with the arrival photo. Once a day per job.

02:27:40.557 --> 02:27:51.857
Accepted online → deposit. When a customer signs the online estimate, the job, contract and payment schedule are made and the deposit invoice is emailed.

02:27:52.357 --> 02:28:00.157
Card declined. Marking a card as declined emails the customer to update it and gives the office a call ticket.

02:28:00.657 --> 02:28:11.823
Satisfaction survey. A short survey link the days you set after a job is complete. A score at or below your number opens a ticket so someone calls the customer.

02:28:12.323 --> 02:28:24.357
Website requests. Off: requests wait on My day for someone to accept. On: genuine-looking ones become a customer and a ticket at once, for the person in "Tickets go to".

02:28:24.857 --> 02:28:32.157
Sent and wording. Each card says how many went out in the last 30 days. Edit wording opens its message.

02:28:32.507 --> 02:28:35.474
Change the wording of an email or text.

02:28:36.174 --> 02:28:43.874
Start from a card. Every automation card has its own wording (the Wording button at the top opens the same place).

02:28:44.374 --> 02:28:49.340
Edit wording. Opens that message. Here: the appointment reminder.

02:28:49.840 --> 02:28:56.107
The message. Its name, and when it was last changed and by whom ("Standard wording" if never).

02:28:56.607 --> 02:29:03.140
Send it. Switches this one message off without stopping its automation. Kept when you press Save wording.

02:29:03.640 --> 02:29:08.307
Subject. The email's subject line. {placeholders} work here too.

02:29:08.807 --> 02:29:15.774
Message. The email text. A blank line starts a new paragraph. The preview follows as you type.

02:29:16.274 --> 02:29:25.740
Placeholders. Click one to put it where the cursor is: first name, appointment day and time, who with, address… Each customer gets their own.

02:29:26.240 --> 02:29:35.707
Text message version. The text version, sent only when texts are switched on. Keep it under 160 characters; the hint counts them.

02:29:36.207 --> 02:29:44.340
Preview. Below: the message as a real customer would get it, with sample numbers. It follows your changes as you type.

02:29:44.840 --> 02:29:48.807
Save wording. Keeps it; the next messages use it.

02:29:49.307 --> 02:29:53.040
Undo changes. Goes back to the saved wording.

02:29:53.540 --> 02:30:04.974
Every message. Every message the system sends, including some with no switch of their own (You're on the schedule, the yearly maintenance price change). "Off" marks one switched off.

02:30:05.474 --> 02:30:08.874
Pick another one. Click a message to change it.

02:30:09.374 --> 02:30:15.674
Button. A message with a link has a button; this is its wording, e.g. View your estimate.

02:30:16.024 --> 02:30:20.491
See what is waiting and what went out (stop or resend a message).

02:30:21.191 --> 02:30:23.924
Queue. Messages waiting to go.

02:30:24.424 --> 02:30:37.957
Waiting to go. Each message, customer, subject and address, and when it goes. The eye shows it, the arrow sends it now, the x cancels it. If its reason goes away (paid, answered) it cancels itself.

02:30:38.457 --> 02:30:40.424
Sent. What went out.

02:30:41.057 --> 02:30:48.124
What went out. The last 80 messages, newest first. Messages marked test went to the test address.

02:30:48.624 --> 02:30:53.724
Not sent. The ones that failed, were cancelled or were skipped, with the reason.

02:30:54.224 --> 02:30:57.491
Send again. Queues that message once more.

02:30:57.991 --> 02:31:00.657
Sent. Only the ones that went out.

02:31:01.157 --> 02:31:03.357
All. Everything again.

02:31:03.857 --> 02:31:07.224
The customer. The name opens the customer.

02:31:07.724 --> 02:31:10.457
View it. The eye shows the message.

02:31:10.957 --> 02:31:18.257
The message. Its subject, who it went (or was meant) to and, if it didn't go, why. Below: the message itself.

02:31:18.757 --> 02:31:21.324
Close it. The tour closes it.

02:31:21.674 --> 02:31:26.074
Set up sending: live email, test address, texts, links.

02:31:26.774 --> 02:31:31.407
Sending setup. The Sending setup tab: how messages are sent.

02:31:31.907 --> 02:31:40.274
Email. While live email is off, everything goes to the test address (a few a day at most) with the real address in the subject.

02:31:40.774 --> 02:31:50.841
Live email to customers. Switch it on once the wording is right: then automations write to real customers. It needs the office email first.

02:31:51.341 --> 02:31:55.474
Test address. Where emails go while live email is off.

02:31:55.974 --> 02:32:01.307
Test emails a day. The most test emails a day while live email is off.

02:32:01.807 --> 02:32:06.907
Where customers write. Shown in every email so replies reach a person.

02:32:07.407 --> 02:32:17.907
Send from our mailbox. Blank: emails come from the Fieldproxy no-reply. Connect the office mailbox in Fieldproxy, then put its account number here.

02:32:18.407 --> 02:32:22.974
Line under the name. The line under the company name in emails.

02:32:23.474 --> 02:32:30.774
Marketing emails per hour. Mailbox providers limit bulk sends; 200 an hour is safe for most.

02:32:31.274 --> 02:32:43.641
Text messages. Switch texts on for appointment reminders, job notices and "we've arrived". Needs the SMS number set up. Customers who reply STOP are never texted again.

02:32:44.141 --> 02:32:48.407
Test mobile number. Where texts go while live email is off.

02:32:48.907 --> 02:32:56.074
Online payment page. Optional: where customers pay a deposit online. Shown after they accept.

02:32:56.574 --> 02:33:02.741
Request form link. The public request form, used by campaign buttons and the website.

02:33:03.241 --> 02:33:08.741
Crew photos. Yes: crews can't start or finish a job without a photo.

02:33:09.241 --> 02:33:16.507
Too far from the job. Starts or finishes further than this from the address (in meters) are flagged on the job.

02:33:17.007 --> 02:33:22.307
Maintenance ahead. How many days ahead maintenance visits are put on the schedule.

02:33:22.807 --> 02:33:33.441
QuickBooks items. The QuickBooks product/service names for invoice lines, deposits and milestones, and maintenance visits, used in the QuickBooks file.

02:33:33.941 --> 02:33:39.507
Save setup. Keeps everything on this tab. It checks the addresses and links first.

02:33:40.057 --> 02:33:47.828
Chapter nineteen. Settings. Company details, money rules, payment schedules and your logo.

02:33:48.028 --> 02:33:50.128
Everything on Settings.

02:33:50.828 --> 02:34:02.061
Settings. Company details, tax, contract terms, payroll, fleet, payment schedules, commission and the text on documents. Only the owner and the office open it.

02:34:02.561 --> 02:34:10.428
Save settings. Nothing here is kept until you press it (payment schedules have their own Save). It checks the numbers first.

02:34:10.928 --> 02:34:19.861
Company. Company name, phone, email, office address, licence line and time zone, printed on estimates, invoices and emails.

02:34:20.361 --> 02:34:29.395
Estimates. How long estimates are valid, the days to the first and second follow-up, and the amount above which a contract needs a signature.

02:34:29.895 --> 02:34:34.961
Sales tax. The NJ sales tax rate added to taxable work.

02:34:35.461 --> 02:34:44.728
Labour cost per crew-hour. What a crew-hour costs you, for the margins on estimates. Job costing uses the burn rates under Reports.

02:34:45.228 --> 02:34:55.228
How commission works. Commission on the job's gross profit or on the sale; earned when the whole job is paid, or on each paid invoice (sale only).

02:34:55.728 --> 02:35:04.961
Card surcharge. The % added to card payments, shown on invoices and contracts. Blank: no surcharge, and it isn't mentioned.

02:35:05.461 --> 02:35:12.228
Extras rate. The rate per man-hour for extra work not in the estimate, printed in the contract terms.

02:35:12.728 --> 02:35:21.495
Late charge. A % a month added to late invoices once a month, once they are late by the days below. Blank = off.

02:35:21.995 --> 02:35:30.028
Payroll. Overtime after how many hours a week, and the ADP company code for the pay-data file from Timesheets.

02:35:30.528 --> 02:35:39.195
Customer notices. Which types of work (crew specializations) get the "you're on the schedule for …" email. Each job can override it.

02:35:39.695 --> 02:35:44.728
Fleet manager. Who gets the Monday due list and the crews' truck reports.

02:35:45.228 --> 02:35:54.595
When "due soon" starts. How close oil and tires (miles), inspections (days) and machine service (engine hours) must be to count as due soon.

02:35:55.095 --> 02:36:00.195
Snow. The units for salt and ice melt, and whether snow work is taxed.

02:36:00.695 --> 02:36:11.761
Payment schedules. The payments an estimate is split into (each picks one, by type of work). Each card shows them and what they come to on a $20,000 job.

02:36:12.261 --> 02:36:19.261
A schedule. Click one to change it. The top line says whether it's the default or which work it is for.

02:36:19.761 --> 02:36:25.561
New schedule. Makes another one. The tour "Set up a payment schedule" shows the editor.

02:36:26.061 --> 02:36:31.495
Commission rates. The rate for everyone, plus any salesperson with their own rate.

02:36:31.995 --> 02:36:40.595
Add a salesperson rate. Adds a row: pick the salesperson and their %. The x removes one. Kept with Save settings.

02:36:41.095 --> 02:36:47.295
Text on documents. The standard terms printed on estimates, and the footer on invoices.

02:36:47.795 --> 02:36:57.461
Open Automations. Follow-ups, reminders, texts and the sending mailbox are set up under Automations, with the wording of every message.

02:36:57.928 --> 02:37:08.595
Live email. Off: every email goes to the test address instead of the customer. Turn it on when ready; it needs the company email. Kept with Save settings.

02:37:09.095 --> 02:37:13.228
Test address. Where emails go while live email is off.

02:37:13.728 --> 02:37:21.028
Customer quote link. Optional: a link customers can open; {token} is replaced for each estimate.

02:37:21.378 --> 02:37:25.578
Set up a payment schedule (deposit, progress payments, final).

02:37:26.278 --> 02:37:35.245
Payment schedules. Each estimate picks one, by type of work. A fixed first deposit is allowed; the percentages share what is left.

02:37:35.745 --> 02:37:40.778
New schedule. Opens the editor with a 30 / 60 / 10 start.

02:37:41.278 --> 02:37:47.245
Name. What it's called on the estimate, e.g. Paver / hardscape (7 payments).

02:37:47.745 --> 02:37:56.911
Default for these types of work. Crew specializations, with commas (hardscape, landscape…). Estimates for that work start with this schedule.

02:37:57.378 --> 02:38:02.545
The default schedule. Tick it for the schedule every other estimate starts with.

02:38:03.045 --> 02:38:13.011
Start from. Ready-made schedules: 30 / 60 / 10, 50 / 50, Deposit + final, Due on receipt. Pick one, then change it.

02:38:13.511 --> 02:38:18.578
Deposit + final. For example a fixed deposit, then the balance.

02:38:19.078 --> 02:38:23.545
One payment. Its number and name, as the customer reads it.

02:38:24.045 --> 02:38:32.711
How much. % of the rest (a share of what's left after fixed amounts), Fixed $ or The balance (whatever is left; only one).

02:38:33.211 --> 02:38:38.545
The amount. Dollars for a fixed payment, a percentage for "% of the rest".

02:38:39.045 --> 02:38:46.045
When it's due. At signing, on receipt, days before the start, when work starts, on completion, or on a date.

02:38:46.545 --> 02:38:51.211
Order. The arrows move a payment up or down; the x removes it.

02:38:51.711 --> 02:38:55.278
Add a payment. Adds another payment at the end.

02:38:55.778 --> 02:39:03.745
Does it add up?. Green when it works. Red says what to fix, e.g. percentages that don't make 100%.

02:39:04.245 --> 02:39:09.145
Save schedule. Saves it. Open estimates can pick it straight away.

02:39:09.645 --> 02:39:13.345
Close the editor. The tour closes it without saving.

02:39:13.845 --> 02:39:17.178
Change one. Click a schedule to change it.

02:39:17.678 --> 02:39:26.045
Delete. Removes it after asking. Open estimates using it go back to their default; signed contracts keep their payments.

02:39:26.545 --> 02:39:29.745
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

02:39:30.095 --> 02:39:34.162
Put your logo on every estimate, invoice and email.

02:39:34.862 --> 02:39:45.228
Logo. Upload your logo, a PNG or JPG with a white or clear background. It goes at the top of every estimate, invoice and email.

02:39:45.728 --> 02:39:54.995
Most days a crew works. Scheduling warns when a crew would work more days than this in a week, for example a Saturday on top of a full week.

02:39:55.495 --> 02:39:59.262
Save settings. Keeps the logo and your changes.

02:39:59.811 --> 02:40:06.046
Chapter twenty. The Guide. Every how-to in one place, inside the app.

02:40:06.246 --> 02:40:08.279
Everything on Guide.

02:40:08.979 --> 02:40:17.113
The Guide. How it all fits together: the path of a job, how to do the everyday things, and what each part of the menu is for.

02:40:17.613 --> 02:40:22.913
Quick tour of the app. Plays a short tour of the main screens, one after another.

02:40:23.413 --> 02:40:28.413
The path of a job. From the first call to the commission, in nine steps.

02:40:28.913 --> 02:40:36.479
Each step opens its screen. Click a step, like 1 · A call or a request, to open the screen where it happens.

02:40:36.946 --> 02:40:43.613
Crew on site. This one happens on the crew's phone. It opens the Schedule, where you see who is where.

02:40:44.113 --> 02:40:50.013
How to …. The everyday jobs, step by step. The bold words are the buttons to press.

02:40:50.513 --> 02:40:55.513
An open how-to. Numbered steps, with who usually does it under the title.

02:40:56.013 --> 02:41:02.079
Take the tour. Plays that how-to on the real screens, pointing at each button, like this tour.

02:41:02.579 --> 02:41:05.846
Show me. Just opens the screen where it happens.

02:41:06.346 --> 02:41:11.613
Open another. Click a title to open it; the one that was open closes.

02:41:12.113 --> 02:41:15.979
Now open. Its steps, and its own Take the tour.

02:41:16.479 --> 02:41:21.846
Where things are. Every part of the menu, what it's for and how often you'll use it.

02:41:22.346 --> 02:41:26.813
Sell. My day, Customers, Appointments, Estimates and Marketing.

02:41:27.313 --> 02:41:32.179
Build. Jobs, Schedule, Maintenance, Deliveries, Snow and Timesheets.

02:41:32.679 --> 02:41:36.946
Money. Invoices and Reports, for people who see money.

02:41:37.446 --> 02:41:43.913
Setup. Catalogue, Fleet and, for the owner and office, Team & crews, Automations and Settings.

02:41:44.413 --> 02:41:50.379
Open a screen. Click a row to open that screen. The tag says how often it's used.

02:41:50.879 --> 02:41:57.646
Help on every screen. Ask in your own words, or pick "Show me everything on this screen" for a tour like this one.

02:41:58.146 --> 02:42:07.313
Search. Finds customers, phones, streets and EST-, JOB- or INV- numbers from any screen (⌘K).

02:42:07.830 --> 02:42:18.801
Chapter twenty-one. The crew phone app. The crew lead's day, a job, visits and calls, the driver's runs, snow, truck problems and hours.

02:42:19.001 --> 02:42:21.434
The crew lead's day on the phone.

02:42:22.134 --> 02:42:32.668
Today. The crew lead's phone. Each morning starts here: your crew, today's jobs, and the one thing to do next. Big buttons, made for gloves and sunshine.

02:42:33.168 --> 02:42:41.501
Who is here today?. Your usual crew is listed. Switch off anyone who didn't come, so their hours and the job costs stay right.

02:42:42.001 --> 02:42:46.968
Start the crew's day. One tap clocks in everyone who is here, at the yard.

02:42:47.468 --> 02:42:57.434
What the crew is doing. Yard, loading, on the road, on the job, unloading, break. One tap moves everyone's time, so the office sees where the day went.

02:42:57.934 --> 02:43:01.768
Leave for the job. The whole crew is now on the road.

02:43:02.268 --> 02:43:06.334
We're here. Opens the job to take the arrival photo.

02:43:06.834 --> 02:43:13.701
The arrival photo. Needed to start: the house and the work area, stamped with the time and where you are.

02:43:14.201 --> 02:43:24.634
Start the job. Records the start with the photo and G.P.S. The customer gets a message that the crew has arrived, and the crew's time moves onto the job.

02:43:25.134 --> 02:43:32.768
Work, photos and notes. What we're doing and the materials to load, the job's photos, and notes for the office.

02:43:33.268 --> 02:43:36.168
Finish the job. When the work is done.

02:43:36.668 --> 02:43:40.834
The finish photo. The finished work, wide enough to see it all.

02:43:41.334 --> 02:43:46.368
A note for the office. Anything left to do, or what the customer said.

02:43:46.868 --> 02:43:51.434
Done. The job is complete, and the office is told straight away.

02:43:51.934 --> 02:43:57.601
Breaks. Break stops the clock on the work. Back to work picks up where the crew left off.

02:43:58.101 --> 02:44:00.801
Back to work. One big button.

02:44:01.301 --> 02:44:07.968
End the day. Tap it twice: it clocks out the whole crew. My hours shows the day as a timeline.

02:44:08.317 --> 02:44:12.850
A job on the phone: materials, photos, notes, problems.

02:44:13.550 --> 02:44:20.117
The job. The job number, the day of the job, the customer and the address, with Directions and Call.

02:44:20.617 --> 02:44:25.450
Directions. Opens maps with the address. Call rings the customer.

02:44:25.950 --> 02:44:33.750
What we're doing. The work, in the office's words, and any note for the crew. No prices: the crew phone never shows money.

02:44:34.250 --> 02:44:40.217
Materials to load. Tap each item when it's on the truck. The office sees what was loaded.

02:44:40.717 --> 02:44:44.884
Photos. The arrival and finish photos, and any you add.

02:44:45.384 --> 02:44:50.050
Add photos. Take as many as you need, add what they show, and save.

02:44:50.550 --> 02:44:55.884
Notes. A note for the office: it shows on the job in the office straight away.

02:44:56.384 --> 02:44:59.584
Write a note. Type it, then Save the note.

02:45:00.084 --> 02:45:08.050
Report a problem. A broken pipe, the wrong pavers, an unhappy customer: it becomes an office ticket, with photos.

02:45:08.550 --> 02:45:13.817
What's wrong. Say what's wrong, add photos if they help, and send it to the office.

02:45:14.167 --> 02:45:16.934
Visits and phone calls on the phone.

02:45:17.600 --> 02:45:23.467
My appointments. Visits, call-backs and tasks the office booked for you, today first.

02:45:23.967 --> 02:45:28.634
A visit. The customer, what it's for and when, with Directions and Call.

02:45:29.134 --> 02:45:34.067
Notes from the visit. What the customer wants, access, the gate code.

02:45:34.567 --> 02:45:37.700
Measurements. Write them as you take them.

02:45:38.200 --> 02:45:43.267
Photos. The yard and the area to quote. They show in the office straight away.

02:45:43.767 --> 02:45:49.867
Save. Everything you saved is on the appointment in the office, for whoever writes the estimate.

02:45:50.367 --> 02:45:56.534
Visit done, estimate pending. The office sees the visit is done and the quote is waiting.

02:45:57.034 --> 02:46:03.400
A phone call. A call shows one big button with the number. Write what was said, then mark it done.

02:46:03.751 --> 02:46:07.418
The driver's runs: deliveries and containers.

02:46:08.118 --> 02:46:13.384
My runs. Deliveries, container drops, pickups and swaps, today first.

02:46:13.884 --> 02:46:18.651
The run. When, the load, the container and the truck, with Directions.

02:46:19.151 --> 02:46:22.518
On my way. The office sees you are on the road.

02:46:23.018 --> 02:46:25.351
A photo. Where you left it.

02:46:25.851 --> 02:46:31.518
Mark it done. Pick the container that went out if it asks, add a note, and mark it done.

02:46:31.867 --> 02:46:35.234
Snow log, truck problems and my hours.

02:46:35.934 --> 02:46:42.700
Snow sites. Every snow site, the ones not done today first. Anyone signed in can log one.

02:46:43.200 --> 02:46:47.334
Times. Time in and time out, like five thirty A.M.

02:46:47.834 --> 02:46:52.800
What was done. Plowed, salted, shoveled walks, calcium: tap each one.

02:46:53.300 --> 02:46:57.000
Save the visit. The office can bill it straight away.

02:46:57.500 --> 02:47:05.067
A truck problem. Pick the truck or machine, say what's wrong, add a photo: the fleet manager gets it straight away.

02:47:05.567 --> 02:47:13.034
My hours. Today, this week and the days worked, with the day as a timeline: yard, road, job and breaks.

02:47:13.584 --> 02:47:27.029
That's the whole system. In the office app, press Help on any screen and ask in your own words, and the tour plays on your own screen, with your own data. The guide site has every step with its picture.
